{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary","id":1377411,"title":"How does your Creation vary?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-30T17:23:35-07:00","id":1377411,"title":"How does your Creation vary?","content":"I'll get the ball rolling.<br /> <br /> In my Creation, in contrast to elementals. The majority of gods lack a way to readily materialize and instead resort to similar methods to ghosts where they speak through their priests or inhabit effigies of themselves and ride them into battle. The definition of effigy is fairly loose so a Field Guardian might jump into a sacrecrow if its people are in danger while a more powerful and successful one might have its worshipers contruct a wicker man for it to stomp around in something akin to a ramshackle warstrider.<br /> <br /> In what ways is your Creation different to canon? I'm talking significant changes where players might have their expectations of the setting challenged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":1115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","user":"The Hug Ninja","date":". 03-31-2020, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T19:31:02-07:00","id":1377439,"title":"","content":"We already have this in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/65219-your-headcanon\">Your Headcanon Thread.</a><br /> <br /> But my changes, I'm a bit more free form with how I display Godblooded, if I want I may have the Children of mighty beings sometimes display Exalted like strength.<br /> <br /> And My Creation may actually be more like a coin then a plane, and the otherside is more a wild Pangea without humans or Gods but with lots of dinosaurs, and maybe elementals. Humans and spirits would have to be stranded here to start up a population. Though sometimes I think I may change it so its more the bottom layer of the deep below Creation, as I have it the Primordials would just plop new layers on Creation in the past anytime they wanted a tableau rasa.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have it that Mars isn't the only one who has placed mysterious do not interfere block on regions, and I added a mini continent on the Northwest called Lahat at the End of the World, with such a do not interfere mark from Saturn, so the Gods there made their own Mini Mount Meru and Min Heaven called Hightpoint/Kalangitan. And it is one of the 7 Heretical hidden heavens on Creation.<br /> <br /> And Soulsteel used to be tied to the lost Incarna of Incarna of Reincarnation the Queen Mother of Paradise, and its sinister aspect may be a result of her falling in the Primordial War.<br /> <br /> And I screw around with way so Mortals can use Martial Arts if I really want to, like planting a Seed of the Perfected Lotus on their Chakra allows them to learn some Martial arts as Evocations. There are similar things for Sorcery like the Satori Key which can be used to unlock your third eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T21:51:54-07:00","id":1377450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377439#post1377439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We already have this in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/65219-your-headcanon\">Your Headcanon Thread.</a><br /> <br /> And My Creation may actually be more like a coin then a plane, and the otherside is more a wild Pangea without humans or Gods but with lots of dinosaurs, and maybe elementals. Humans and spirits would have to be stranded here to start up a population. Though sometimes I think I may change it so its more the bottom layer of the deep below Creation, as I have it the Primordials would just plop new layers on Creation in the past anytime they wanted a tableau rasa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any chance for a still-in-their-prime Dragon King empire down there? Also, how aware of this &quot;other side of Creation&quot; is Yu-Shan, or the Sidereals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":12975,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","user":"Zealot_Vedas","date":". 03-31-2020, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T22:03:18-07:00","id":1377451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zealot_Vedas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377450#post1377450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any chance for a still-in-their-prime Dragon King empire down there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I was thinking of Offshoot Dragon Kings from earlier layers of Creation Surviving, but limited by their number of souls maybe, haven't decided on how many, and after the Primordial War an unknown pilgrimage of Dragon Kings made expedition down below. Once you surface Pangaea side you use a primordial precursor to Lethe, one that is a bit more potent being able to shift mortals to animals and vice versa. Their legend has it some caveman level humans used to live there but they eventually all got reincarnated as beasts, with their saints becoming Dragon Kings. So they have at least one Dragon King Kingdom but they don't have human slave, unless gamewise the circles follows the lead of a Merchant Prince trying to find this Hollow Earth and discovering he sold his caravan into slavedom.<br /> <br /> I was waiting for 3rd ed to cover Kings. But I do have plans using Melissa Uran's (the Artist) idea for Tonberry's (from Final Fantasy) as Dragon King Litches and I plan to try them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T03:01:52-07:00","id":1377481,"title":"","content":"Okay...<br /> So, thousands of years ago a group of priests of the Titans were helped by Autocthon to steal the power of the Unconquered Sun, becoming the Solar Anathema; immortal spirits who possess heroic mortals. They convinced Gaia, Luna, etc, to betray the Titans. Leading a host of Exalted, they overthrew the Titans.<br /> <br /> However, eventually the Dragons could not stand the Solars anymore. With the help of their Dragonblood armies, the Immaculate Dragons trapped the Solars in Hell with the Titans. However, in this great war the Solars used their magic to utterly destroy the Sidereals (who'd joined the Dragon's cause). Sidereals no longer exist as even a memory. <br /> <br /> As the Lunars had stayed loyal to the Solars, the Dragonblood battled them for 1500 years. But then the sorcerer-queen Raksi and her pack managed to free the Solars from Hell and unleash them on the Realm.<br /> <br /> The Solars, wielding infernal powers learnt from 1500 years in Hell, soon destroyed the Realm. They besieged many of the Realm's greatest heroes on the Imperial Mountain, eventually defeating them, traveling into the Mountain, and killing Pasiap. This caused earthquakes across the world for decades, as well as more metaphysical changes, as Pasiap was Gaia's fetich soul.<br /> Covens of Solars travelled to the other Elemental Poles to wreak vengeance on the other Dragons for their imprisonment. Hesiesh died to Solar infernalism.<br /> <br /> With this, Mela decided to strike back, attempting to destroy humanity with an eternal winter that lasted decades. Some brave Lunar PCs managed to convince her to stop though, in return for helping her kill a Solar assassination team and capture one of the Solar leaders, Yurgen Kaneko.<br /> So, for the last few decades things have been slowly getting warmer, but with several Immaculate Dragons dead, and after a short Ice Age, things look very different.<br /> (But I will have to leave it there for now, as that's as much as the PCs know)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T03:37:23-07:00","id":1377482,"title":"","content":"A major argument in favor of the Usurpation is due to the Ch'Asca Empire, a First Age Empire led by Solars God-Kings, Aztech-Voodoo style, whose empire was so big and who were so powerful that the other Celestial were resorting more and more to extreme violence and solutions to protect themselves from the Ch'Asca, thus &quot;proving&quot; the Solars were unable to master themselves and convincing a lot of Sidereals to support the Usurpation. <br /> <br /> You can find ruins and remnants of the Ch'Asca civilization almost everywhere you go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T04:35:26-07:00","id":1377489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377439#post1377439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We already have this in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/65219-your-headcanon\">Your Headcanon Thread.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I was unclear about what I was looking for, a downside of posting after 1am. I'm more interested in the sort of changes to the setting that your PCs actively grapple with rather than the sort of setting changes that could be introduced by establishing a fact.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T04:59:08-07:00","id":1377495,"title":"","content":"I think Headcanon is a bit different to &quot;my Creation&quot;. I mean, the above stuff I mentioned is very different to the previous game I ran.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T06:46:20-07:00","id":1377508,"title":"","content":"I think that the Biggest Change currently in our Game is that the Cult of the Illuminated have gone public and have become somewhat powerful, if not influential - The Illuminated Order is opposed to the Immaculate Faith. It is an interesting dynamic... though the Illuminated Order has been restructured a bit from 1st Edition... I was never a fan of the 1st Edition Cult - the Sidereal have far less power in our version, and the Order is definitely a more responsible religion in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-31-2020, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T06:55:37-07:00","id":1377509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377439#post1377439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But my changes, I'm a bit more free form with how I display Godblooded, if I want I may have the Children of mighty beings sometimes display Exalted like strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the caveat that what I mean by &quot;Exalted like strength&quot; and what you mean by it are probably very different: yoink.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377439#post1377439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I screw around with way so Mortals can use Martial Arts if I really want to, like planting a Seed of the Perfected Lotus on their Chakra allows them to learn some Martial arts as Evocations. There are similar things for Sorcery like the Satori Key which can be used to unlock your third eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>Double yoink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-31-2020, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T01:20:21-07:00","id":1377683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377509#post1377509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the caveat that what I mean by &quot;Exalted like strength&quot; and what you mean by it are probably very different: yoink.<br /> <br /> <br /> Double yoink.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it'd be more interesting that you present your own ideas rather than just coming to criticize others without giving any actual content","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T02:07:35-07:00","id":1377692,"title":"","content":"He's not criticising, he's yoinking (with caveats).<br /> <br /> So this is my latest map, to show what locals told the PCs.<br /> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/tZFhr2x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/5Yw9Hjn/Nice-map.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> Bear in mind that big forest is where they are... and based on accents, they think they're near Gethemene.<br /> <br /> Compare that to the map of the North...<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://howsfamily.net/Exalted/map/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://howsfamily.net/Exalted/map/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://howsfamily.net/Exalted/map/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://howsfamily.net/Exalted/map/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The mountains do kind of match the central North. But that's nowhere near Iscomay.<br /> <br /> Because, well... most of the PCs have terrible Lore. One has good Lore, but is from far in the far North-East, so geography isn't really his background (compared to, say, herbs).<br /> So why should their knowledge of geography be anachronistically good? Why should geography look like what it does on the Exalted Map?<br /> So there's all sorts of random changes everywhere, except near where the game started. Nexus is a tree-city (because it's in the East) for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","e