Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T03:16:43-07:00","id":1377698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377695#post1377695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Yoink is the onomatopoeia for stealing something.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s <i>an</i> onomatopoeia for stealing something, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T04:18:33-07:00","id":1377707,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t have my own Creation, but the guy who taught me about Exalted, his version of Creation is a pocket dimension in the middle of the Flux Realm (one of the Near Umbral Realms from Werewolf: the Apocalypse). Also, his version is an ellipse, with the West and East Poles at the two vertices of the eclipse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T04:19:16-07:00","id":1377708,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> it\u2019s also from Scooby-Doo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T04:21:07-07:00","id":1377710,"title":"","content":"* ellipse. Not eclipse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T11:10:08-07:00","id":1377765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377683#post1377683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it'd be more interesting that you present your own ideas rather than just coming to criticize others without giving any actual content</div> </div> </div> </div>My Creation is pretty much set in the default setting with a bit more of the blank edges of the map filled in... but sure.<br /> <br /> In my Creation there are secret tunnels built just before the War of the Gods. Some by the gods for their Exalted champions. Some by other beings for other purposes.<br /> <br /> The game is mostly set East of Jiara around a First Age city/ruin called Urza Arcus amidst the broken wonders of the Solars (including a mystic portal to other dimensions -- certainly The Underworld and Malfeas and perhaps others).<br /> <br /> Thunderbirds are still found in the West, but unusually this Eastern city has one.<br /> <br /> Lookshyans, being Shogunate remnants, speak High Realm (stylized with Japanese honorifics and the occasional loan word).<br /> <br /> Uh... there's a manse that lets people pull artifacts out of their soul.<br /> <br /> God-blooded vary tremendously in power. Estoric means exist for mortals to gain power. One of the main antagonists is a god-blood who became a Deathknight after a (well, several) botched attempt(s) to gain power -- whether this means god-blooded can increase their power through estoric ritual (and whether Exalted can) is thus left deliberately ambiguous (I'm leaning &quot;no&quot;, And The Gift of Merciful Silence just got (un)lucky).<br /> <br /> High Realm is stylized as English. River Speak is stylized as French. Old Realm is generally stylized as Xhosa, Latin, Greek and any other language I might care to throw in, but demonic speach is stylized as cockney/KSBD English (for 1CDs) or late Elizabthian (2CDs). Might stylize Low Realm as German. [Edit: Flametongue is Spanish. Which is awkward as I don't actually speak Spanish. I've so far managed to bluff with song lyrics.] This generally means funny accents and the odd loan word when RPing, it's not an in-universe conceit. Although...<br /> <br /> And I think that's about it. Throne still empty, no civil war yet. Haven't killed off any Elemental Dragons or anything like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-05-2020, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T02:49:18-07:00","id":1377914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377695#post1377695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh this is a misunderstanding. I think Yoink is the onomatopoeia for stealing something. I reckon he means he likes the idea and plans to use it. So its a compliment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> Oh I'm sorry then I should have checked the meaning of yoink before posting, my sincere apologies","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T03:47:29-07:00","id":1377920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377914#post1377914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> Oh I'm sorry then I should have checked the meaning of yoink before posting, my sincere apologies</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. IT means that your stuff is so good, that people want to take it for themselves. <br /> <br /> A pretty good flattery .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T04:11:17-07:00","id":1377922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377914#post1377914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> Oh I'm sorry then I should have checked the meaning of yoink before posting, my sincere apologies</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple miscommunication and your intentions were clearly positive in that they were in defense of others so its truly a harmless mistake. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T06:19:08-07:00","id":1377939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377765#post1377765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Creation is pretty much set in the default setting with a bit more of the blank edges of the map filled in... but sure.<br /> <br /> In my Creation there are secret tunnels built just before the War of the Gods. Some by the gods for their Exalted champions. Some by other beings for other purposes.<br /> <br /> The game is mostly set East of Jiara around a First Age city/ruin called Urza Arcus amidst the broken wonders of the Solars (including a mystic portal to other dimensions -- certainly The Underworld and Malfeas and perhaps others).<br /> <br /> Thunderbirds are still found in the West, but unusually this Eastern city has one.<br /> <br /> Lookshyans, being Shogunate remnants, speak High Realm (stylized with Japanese honorifics and the occasional loan word).<br /> <br /> Uh... there's a manse that lets people pull artifacts out of their soul.<br /> <br /> God-blooded vary tremendously in power. Estoric means exist for mortals to gain power. One of the main antagonists is a god-blood who became a Deathknight after a (well, several) botched attempt(s) to gain power -- whether this means god-blooded can increase their power through estoric ritual (and whether Exalted can) is thus left deliberately ambiguous (I'm leaning &quot;no&quot;, And The Gift of Merciful Silence just got (un)lucky).<br /> <br /> High Realm is stylized as English. River Speak is stylized as French. Old Realm is generally stylized as Xhosa, Latin, Greek and any other language I might care to throw in, but demonic speach is stylized as cockney/KSBD English (for 1CDs) or late Elizabthian (2CDs). Might stylize Low Realm as German. This generally means funny accents and the odd loan word when RPing, it's not an in-universe conceit. Although...<br /> <br /> And I think that's about it. Throne still empty, no civil war yet. Haven't killed off any Elemental Dragons or anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh Now its our turn to Yoink!<br /> <br /> I always am for more backstory for the Underground of Creation so I am Nabbing that. In my game's secret History their were 108 prototype Unconquered Suns buried at the core of Creation deep below, and the first Sun Prototype zero is the All Conquering Sun which the Primordials figured they made too mighty so all Suns after were toned down. The others varied drastically in power and they experimented even in their natures so some are Behemoths rather then Gods.<br /> <br /> Its rather inspired how you handled Hell's dialects particularly, I like the intent and I will adopt some aspects of that. Do you attribute a particular accent to Yu-Shan?<br /> <br /> And More on the Manse that allows you to pull artifacts out of your soul, is it a Solar Manse? Is it Rating N/A? Just that simple sentence inspires me, I love reasons for custom artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T13:26:25-07:00","id":1378029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377939#post1377939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its rather inspired how you handled Hell's dialects particularly, I like the intent and I will adopt some aspects of that. Do you attribute a particular accent to Yu-Shan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you seen Disney's Mary Poppins? Mr. Banks.<br /> <br /> Snooty, Edwardian, upper class, English. &quot;I dare say, old chap. What? Pip pip! Right-o, jolly good!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377939#post1377939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And More on the Manse that allows you to pull artifacts out of your soul, is it a Solar Manse? Is it Rating N/A? Just that simple sentence inspires me, I love reasons for custom artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in Dynasty of Dovak there are only two artifacts that have been &quot;successfully&quot; manufactured by the manse (that I'm aware of, anyway). One is a custom Artifact 5 (possibly N/A) daiklave wielded by an NPC antagonist who has only appeared in flashbacks thusfar. The other is a reskinned Fist of Titans used by my character.<br /> <br /> We're actually visiting the manse for the first time in a flashback next session, but here's what we knocked out for background:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Lost Manse \u2013 Greater Earth Aspected Manse<br /> <br /> Sidereal Records: Raised in the Third Epoch of the Shogunate in the year of the Iron Wolverine atop an Earth Aspected demesne, this seven story ziggurat is notable for being raised by [Redacted by Order of Heaven]. Its exact location was lost to the records of Heaven, certainly after the Great Contagion though some senior figures in the Bureau of Secrets suspect the record to have been redacted long before that. The original name of the manse is unknown.<br /> <br /> The manse was raised under Sidereal supervision in an attempt to counter-act the increasing decline in the Shogunate\u2019s ability to produce artifacts. Involvement of [Redacted by Order of Heaven] was deemed undesirable, but necessary in order to overcome [Redacted by Order of Heaven] [\u2026]<br /> <br /> [Redacted by Order of Heaven] but ultimately, the project was considered a failure. In the 3<sup>rd</sup> Year of the Mercury Mospid, the manse was sealed with five jade keys, its control hearthstone secured within the manse\u2019s deepest level.<br /> <br /> The Manse has one entrance, at the upmost level of the ziggurat. Aspirants attempting Transubstantive Artifact Generation must enter through the top of the manse and work their way to the core, where the concentration of Earth Essence is strongest. The esoteric inclusion of [Redacted by Order of Heaven] in the manse\u2019s construction, combined with the control key that serves as the manse\u2019s hearthstone, in theory makes the process of drawing forth an artifact from the Essence of One\u2019s Being possible.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Records follow.<br /> <br /> Lookshy Records Begin: In the 10<sup>th</sup> Year of the Copper Carp, Amilar Shavok founds the (later proscribed terrorist group) The Seekers of Eternal Truth. Founding members are all apprentices at the Valkhawsen Academy of Sorcery, including Outcasts Mighty Hawk, Crashes the Surf, Nerigus Saman and Karal Senari. Senari is killed during proscribed rituals undertaken by the Seekers (in order to attempt to prove Shavok\u2019s theories of Transubstantive Artifact Generation) in the Year of the Copper Serpent, and the group is officially disbanded: Lorja Mighty Hawk, Kinsh Crashes the Surf and Nerigus Saman are expelled from the Valkhawsen, though Amilar Shavok escapes censor thanks to the intervention of his uncle Taimyo Amilar Zochu. Shavok\u2019s theories lead the Seekers on their quest to uncover the Lost Manse, and they piece together fragmentary Shogunate records alongside Seventh Legion field reports.<br /> <br /> In the Year of the Copper Dolphin, Seventh Year exchange student Cynis Ganan transfers to the Valkhawsen from the Heptagram. Ganan is inducted into the Seekers of Eternal Truth, and goes on to locate the Lost Manse. The Seekers make their way to the manse, and fight their way through the trials.<br /> <br /> In attempting Transubstantive Artifact Generation, the Seekers mostly die in various horrific ways. Kinsh Crashes the Surf collapses as raw molten orichalcum pours from her every orifice (the orichalcum is later recovered by the Seventh Legion). Lorja Mighty Hawk\u2019s body is found impaled on fractured shards of blue jade: the shards are held in his hands, protruding from his chest, looking almost as if he stabbed himself in the chest. Nerigus Saman\u2019s skin is found in a puddle: their bones transformed into a mess of tangled thorny brambles and pulled through a gaping hole in their chest, pulling their organs out as well \u2013 no traces of magical materials are found within the twisted combination of plant and Dragon-Blood. Of Amilar Shavok there is no sign. Cynis Ganan survives, his body wracked by sorcerous energy, leaving him unable to walk and grievously injured.<br /> <br /> The Lost Manse implodes, a wounded Cynis Ganan drags his shattered body twenty miles where it is found by a Sijanese convoy \u2013 he is returned to the Realm after thorough interrogation. The manse\u2019s keys are recovered by the Seventh Legion, but the manse\u2019s hearthstone is missing. Amilar Shavok declared Anathema. Detailed accounts of the \u201cShavok Incident\u201d are kept at the Valkhawsen, standing orders for a Wyld Hunt against Shavok remain in place (as of the 11<sup>th</sup> Year of the Bronze Mouse), and a redoubt is located at the site of the Lost Manse: the implosion damage and loss of the hearthstone renders the manse inoperable (and the General Staff have no intention of restoring the manse).<br /> <br /> Realm Records Begin: In Realm Year 725, Cynis Ganan transfers to the Valkhawsen Academy of Sorcery. The renowned First Age Historian easily uncovers a lost Shogunate era manse, but is tragically wounded when betrayed by the disgraced Mad Sorcerer Amilar Shavok. After an unjustly lengthy interrogation by the Seventh Legion, Ganan is returned to the Realm wielding the white-and-blue jade tetsubo Thunder\u2019s Crash.<br /> <br /> Thunder\u2019s Crash is a deceptively simplistic weapon that appears to be carved from a solid block of white jade, banded in pure blue jade and wrapped in a simple leather thonging with hearthstone slots in the hilt and pommel. By all tests conducted by the Heptagram, it appears to be a \u201cnormal\u201d artifact which embodies destructive, smashing forces. Cynis Ganan claims that he was able to draw forth the weapon from his chest using \u201cTransubstantive Artifact Generation\u201d at the site of the Lost Manse. The process all-but-killed the Earth Aspect, who was renowned for his great physical strength and unparalleled constitution. It would take some 18 years for Ganan to recover from his injuries sufficiently to walk unaided, and as of Realm Year 768 he still has yet to recover his famed constitution, and he remains scarred by swirling mystic sigils that echo his aspect markings. The Realm maintains a standing order of Wyld Hunt against Amilar Shavok, though he hasn't been seen in 43 years.<br /> <br /> A detailed account is believed to be kept at the Heptagram.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> One of the players threw an epic fit that we were going to do the maiming of my PC without them. So we didn't actually end up playing this out in depth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-05-2020, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T17:47:41-07:00","id":1379557,"title":"","content":"*Heterodox Take Warning*<br /> <br /> In my Creation, rather than a corrupt, incompetent, baby-eating rape machine of ignorant evil, the Realm is structured to create the opportunity for reasonable people (celestial exalts) to disagree about whether the Realm should be toppled. For instance:<ul><li>My Realm is one of the most gender-equitable nations on Creation (because it's ruled by a bunch of people with lots of magic power unrelated to gender)</li> <li>My Realm employs something more like a modern-day China approach (belt and road, investing in foreign resources to extract them, etc.) and US approach (control US denominated foreign debt, international economic systems, etc.) than Empire (whatever the capital &quot;E&quot; and lack of article is supposed to mean here)</li> <li>The Vision of Bronze and Vision of Gold more clearly and explicitly defined in terms of Bronze = high change of moderate outcome, low chance of disaster and Gold = low chance of amazing outcome, high chance of disaster so that reasonable people can disagree based on risk tolerance. (Expected utility of Bronze is higher, but potential maximum utility of Gold is higher)</li> <li>The Immaculate Philosophy isn't 90% nonsense. Instead, it's 90% about enforcing the metaphysical order that actually makes Creation run well (making sure that Gods get prayer efficiently, that they're doing what they're supposed to do, etc.) and 10% about enforcing the rule of the Scarlet Dynasty, but in a way that relies on a philosophy of social (and global) harmony.</li> <li>Etc.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T18:32:42-07:00","id":1379564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1379557#post1379557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Heterodox Take Warning*<br /> <br /> In my Creation, rather than a corrupt, incompetent, baby-eating rape machine of ignorant evil, the Realm</div> </div> </div> </div>Why... do you feel the need to do this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T23:21:50-07:00","id":1379652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1379557#post1379557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my Creation, rather than a corrupt, incompetent, baby-eating rape machine of ignorant evil, the Realm is structured to create the opportunity for reasonable people (celestial exalts) to disagree about whether the Realm should be toppled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not convinced you're getting that outcome.<br /> It seems like the reasonable person should see that toppling your version of the Realm rather than reforming it is a huge mistake that'll kill millions from loss of infastructure and warlords rising to fill a power vaccum. Unfortunately lot of Celestial Exalt aren't exactly reasonable and trying to murder them before they become too powerful doesn't exactly help with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T23:55:54-07:00","id":1379670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1379557#post1379557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Heterodox Take Warning*<br /> <br /> In my Creation, rather than a corrupt, incompetent, baby-eating rape machine of ignorant evil, the Realm is structured to create the opportunity for reasonable people (celestial exalts) to disagree about whether the Realm should be toppled. For instance:<ul><li>My Realm is one of the most gender-equitable nations on Creation (because it's ruled by a bunch of people with lots of magic power unrelated to gender)</li> <li>My Realm employs something more like a modern-day China approach (belt and road, investing in foreign resources to extract them, etc.) and US approach (control US denominated foreign debt, international economic systems, etc.) than Empire (whatever the capital &amp;quot;E&amp;quot; and lack of article is supposed to mean here)</li> <li>The Vision of Bronze and Vision of Gold more clearly and explicitly defined in terms of Bronze = high change of moderate outcome, low chance of disaster and Gold = low chance of amazing outcome, high chance of disaster so that reasonable people can disagree based on risk tolerance. (Expected utility of Bronze is higher, but potential maximum utility of Gold is higher)</li> <li>The Immaculate Philosophy isn't 90% nonsense. Instead, it's 90% about enforcing the metaphysical order that actually makes Creation run well (making sure that Gods get prayer efficiently, that they're doing what they're supposed to do, etc.) and 10% about enforcing the rule of the Scarlet Dynasty, but in a way that relies on a philosophy of social (and global) harmony.</li> <li>Etc.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this basically canon?<br /> <br /> The Dynasty was (1/2E) pretty explicitly a gender neutral meritocracy. 3E dials up the sexism a little, but it's still pretty much within the tolerances set by modern, Western society.<br /> <br /> Several Satrapies are portrayed as investments. The Realm gouging its tributaries is seen as a recent insult as the Houses gear up for civil war.<br /> <br /> That is literally, explicitly what the Visions of Bronze and Gold were. After the world was nearly destroyed by the Great Contagion and the Deathknights were unleashed, the math changed a little, but the principals are the same: do we take the high risk/high reward option of letting the Solars roam free, or the high cost/low risk option of Dragon-Blooded rule? And is the question even still relevant, or are Federalists debating Whigs at this point?<br /> <br /> Whether the Immaculate Order's take on reincarnation is true is ambiguous at best... but otherwise, yeah, it's the religion that dominates the world. It's supposed to be functional.<br /> <br /> (I mean, if you think China and the USA aren't corrupt and incompetent... I really don't know what to tell you. Quote post me in Offtopic if you like, but I'm not going to have a political debate in this thread.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T00:52:38-07:00","id":1379693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1379670#post1379670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I mean, if you think China and the USA aren't corrupt and incompetent... I really don't know what to tell you. Quote post me in Offtopic if you like, but I'm not going to have a political debate in this thread.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, It's the comparing the Realm to modern-day America and China that informed my reading of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T01:38:53-07:00","id":1379709,"title":"","content":"The first paragraph informed me of it. Maybe previous editions really depicted the Realm as the Ultimate Forces of Evil, but I literally cannot understand someone thinking the Realm is a &quot;corrupt, incompetent, baby eating rape machine of ignorant evil&quot; given 3e descriptions. Some of its individuals and organizations are clearly ill-intentioned, but I don't see how it justify saying &quot;then the whole organization is Evil and everything they do is terrible&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T03:11:41-07:00","id":1379718,"title":"","content":"Actually Chausse, the reason for that post is that some people think that the Realm has been made much worse in <i>this</i> edition, compared to 2nd ed. I don't really think so (Sesus Chenow's gone, for one thing), but I guess Equitable Remedy does.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, moving on, as that looks like Headcanon and not &quot;My Creation.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, in my chronicle, which is called &quot;Lunars: The Apocalypse&quot;, there was an apocalypse (well, a pretty small one as apocalypses go, but still). The Realm and many other societies* were destroyed, and only a few old states survive, though in different forms.<br /> <br /> So here's some maps of the North as it is now.<br /> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/djgsqph\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/34z5qFJ/Nice-map.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/bd1kYrs\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/zfszCSX/The-big-north.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/zGZ2pkJ\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/Rzc6f5y/Migration-era.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> The last one isn't what it looks like know, just showing where the people went. I do kind of like the late antiquity period after all.<br /> <br /> Note that Diamond Hearth and Icehome are on that second map, because the PCs visited them, but they're actually ruined and completely abandoned.<br /> <br /> *Meta-commentary:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">All the states from 1st and 2nd edition happen to be amongst those which have been destroyed, while some of the new 3rd edition states are amongst those which still survive. We've played Exalted for 13 years, I wanted a change. I don't really like places like Whitewall, Gethamane, Nexus, etc, anyway, but even the stuff I do find interesting, such as the Realm, Cherak, the Lintha, An-Teng, the Haslanti League, etc, are all gone. Because after 13 years, they're a bit dull. Especially as I play two other long-running Exalted games anyway.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-09-2020, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T04:46:41-07:00","id":1380082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1379709#post1379709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first paragraph informed me of it. Maybe previous editions really depicted the Realm as the Ultimate Forces of Evil, but I literally cannot understand someone thinking the Realm is a &amp;quot;corrupt, incompetent, baby eating rape machine of ignorant evil&amp;quot; given 3e descriptions. Some of its individuals and organizations are clearly ill-intentioned, but I don't see how it justify saying &amp;quot;then the whole organization is Evil and everything they do is terrible&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really about what's in the books, it's about online discourse that took place in the years of anticipating the books.<br /> <br /> Plus other things better off not being discussed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T08:04:34-07:00","id":1380119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1380082#post1380082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not really about what's in the books, it's about online discourse that took place in the years of anticipating the books.<br /> <br /> Plus other things better off not being discussed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You got me curious about the other things better off not being discussed but I guess it'll stay as a mystery.<br /> <br /> In my Creation, the V'neef decided to not commit fully to the throne race and went instead to try and invade the Dreaming Sea. I took the decision at a time where I had no idea what the houses were about individually, and it happened I think it fits well enough I kept this idea for other later campaigns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T16:16:52-07:00","id":1383052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377765#post1377765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Creation is pretty much set in the default setting with a bit more of the blank edges of the map filled in... but sure.<br /> <br /> In my Creation there are secret tunnels built just before the War of the Gods. Some by the gods for their Exalted champions. Some by other beings for other purposes.<br /> <br /> The game is mostly set East of Jiara around a First Age city/ruin called Urza Arcus amidst the broken wonders of the Solars (including a mystic portal to other dimensions -- certainly The Underworld and Malfeas and perhaps others).<br /> <br /> Thunderbirds are still found in the West, but unusually this Eastern city has one.<br /> <br /> Lookshyans, being Shogunate remnants, speak High Realm (stylized with Japanese honorifics and the occasional loan word).<br /> <br /> Uh... there's a manse that lets people pull artifacts out of their soul.<br /> <br /> God-blooded vary tremendously in power. Estoric means exist for mortals to gain power. One of the main antagonists is a god-blood who became a Deathknight after a (well, several) botched attempt(s) to gain power -- whether this means god-blooded can increase their power through estoric ritual (and whether Exalted can) is thus left deliberately ambiguous (I'm leaning &quot;no&quot;, And The Gift of Merciful Silence just got (un)lucky).<br /> <br /> High Realm is stylized as English. River Speak is stylized as French. Old Realm is generally stylized as Xhosa, Latin, Greek and any other language I might care to throw in, but demonic speach is stylized as cockney/KSBD English (for 1CDs) or late Elizabthian (2CDs). Might stylize Low Realm as German. This generally means funny accents and the odd loan word when RPing, it's not an in-universe conceit. Although...<br /> <br /> And I think that's about it. Throne still empty, no civil war yet. Haven't killed off any Elemental Dragons or anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also:<br /> <br /> Cynis is the child of the Empress and Tepet.<br /> <br /> This is important because Tepet Igan is from a Cynis bloodline that married back into Tepet, causing some confusion over whether V'neef's husband is a Tepet or &quot;one of the wealthier and less decadent Cynis&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also Ragara Bhagwei is the child of Cynis and Ragara, but almost no-one knows that.<br /> <br /> Also the Realm is responsible for the trade war between Gem and Paragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T23:15:58-07:00","id":1383099,"title":"","content":"I love magitech, I game with two groups who have all played FF6, and so in my games there are warstriders on the regular. One is a Dragon-Blooded game where the players pilot the warstriders. Another is a Solars game where they're trying to stand up a kingdom resilient enough to handle warstrider aggro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T05:52:42-07:00","id":1383132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1383052#post1383052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Ragara Bhagwei is the child of Cynis and Ragara, but almost no-one knows that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seen zero indication that's changed.<br /> Just that in his parentage wasn't considered important for the paragraph of characterisation he has as the Heptagram's dominie and less important in Ex3 overall.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T07:41:12-07:00","id":1383141,"title":"","content":"In my gaming group most of Creation is pretty standard, the cross-pollination of players across several groups has lead to a pretty cannon Creation...with one exception. By now it is tradition that Ydanna is something weird and different every time we play, established by lore roll and group world-building. This originally started because it is labeled on the map but there isn't anything about it in the core, at this point I quite like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T08:28:50-07:00","id":1383144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1383132#post1383132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seen zero indication that's changed.<br /> Just that in his parentage wasn't considered important for the paragraph of characterisation he has as the Heptagram's dominie and less important in Ex3 overall.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In 1E, all three Cynis sisters know as does Banoba and whomever he was telling the peach story to.<br /> 1E and 2E, Bhagwei himself knows.<br /> <br /> 3E Bhagwei's parentage is unstated.<br /> <br /> My Creation, Ragara knows, O Nama knows. That's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T13:49:20-07:00","id":1383207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1383144#post1383144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1E, all three Cynis sisters know as does Banoba and whomever he was telling the peach story to.<br /> 1E and 2E, Bhagwei himself knows.<br /> <br /> 3E Bhagwei's parentage is unstated.<br /> <br /> My Creation, Ragara knows, O Nama knows. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cynis was biological daughter of the Empress, and I should be this grossed out, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T14:20:49-07:00","id":1383220,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's why it was secret.<br /> <br /> (Bit weird that Ragara claimed him and not Cynis. You'd think it'd be easier to cover up for Cynis. But maybe she just didn't want him.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T14:29:49-07:00","id":1383223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1383141#post1383141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my gaming group most of Creation is pretty standard, the cross-pollination of players across several groups has lead to a pretty cannon Creation...with one exception. By now it is tradition that Ydanna is something weird and different every time we play, established by lore roll and group world-building. This originally started because it is labeled on the map but there isn't anything about it in the core, at this point I quite like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My group did the same thing back in the early 1e days with Kirigast. Which went virtually the entire product line for 1e until Houses of the Bull God came out. <br /> <br /> My favorite iteration was someone doing up a city that erased itself from your memory after you left, which is why Kirigast appeared as early as 2001's map of Creation but not a single explanation was ever cited in canon until 2004 or 2005. Ah good times...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11870-epiphany","name":"Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T14:32:35-07:00","id":1383224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1383220#post1383220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's why it was secret.<br /> <br /> (Bit weird that Ragara claimed him and not Cynis. You'd think it'd be easier to cover up for Cynis. But maybe she just didn't want him.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know I get the feeling 3rd ed wants to distance themselves from the icky stuff...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T14:33:43-07:00","id":1383225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1383207#post1383207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cynis was biological daughter of the Empress, and I should be this grossed out, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes.<br /> <br /> Cynis's father (and/or second mother) is unstated. I like Tepet for her father.<br /> <br /> Ragara's father is Rawar. So she's Ragara's half-sister.<br /> <br /> And Bhagwei isn't part of his mother's House. So there's a weird power dynamic there as well as the casual incest.<br /> <br /> Plus, Ragara is (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/65219-your-headcanon?p=1340505#post1340505\">according to my headcanon, at least</a>) like 119 years older than Cynis (if Cynis is the daughter of Tepet, then her birth coinciding with the Empress stripping the Shogunate gens of their special privilidges makes sense -- it also makes sense as to why House Cynis isn't a thing until over 116 years after Cynis's adult son graduates the Versino -- because Gens Tepet is still prestigious. So you can tell we're lowballing this age-gap, but it does at least put Cynis at 96 to Ragara's 215 so she's lived an entire mortal lifetime before having her brother's child).<br /> <br /> A relationship between Tepet Cynis and Ragara also explains why he doesn't show her the emnity he shows Mnemon -- Tepet was only a consort, and it's not like (to Ragara's mind) Cynis will ever found her own Great House to rival him.<br /> <br /> And it <i>kinda </i>explains how Ragara gets the boy, if Cynis has to answer to her Gens leadership (especially as her father is likely yet to go missing before Bhagwei's birth) and Ragara considers his Great House to be closer to the Empress than a Shogunate Gens stripped of its special privileges.<br /> <br /> Canon Dates<br /> <br /> 139 Birth of Ragara (The Realm)<br /> 266 Shogunate Gens stripped (The Realm)<br /> 369 Birth of Mnemon (The Realm)<br /> 385 Destruction of Versino (1E, 2E, Mnemon remains age 16 in 3E timeline)<br /> 399 Sesus born (The Realm)<br /> 428 Ragara Bhagwei founds the Heptagram (1E Aspect Book Wood, 2E)<br /> 501 House Cynis elevated (The Realm)<br /> &quot;Centuries before 768&quot; Cynis dies of heroin and dreamdust overdose (What Fire Hath Wrought)<br /> <br /> This gives us anywhere between 139 and 359 for the birth of Cynis (if she remains the mother of Bhagwei). And anywhere between 363 and 371 for the birth of Ragara Bhagwei (assuming he still attended the Versino as a contemporary of Mnemon and founded the Heptagram).<br /> <br /> I favor 266 for Cynis and 364 for Bhagwei.<br /> <br /> Worth noting that Sesus is now younger than Mnemon, and Ragara's sibling killing spree now ended some time after 399. Making it not unlikely that he had a hand in Cynis's death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-22-2020, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T02:51:01-07:00","id":1385225,"title":"","content":"So, here's the North-East you're all familiar with (ignore the arrows).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/Y4KNs3Rk\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/Y4KNs3Rk/Travel-map.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> Well, my PCs went to the Elemental Pole of Air to end Fimbulwinter, which of course meant travelling through the Wyld. And when they returned from the lands of Faerie, 100 years had passed. The Haslanti cities are abandoned, frozen ruins. The nation of Iscomay has pretty much entirely migrated south-east. Linowan has entirely flooded. A lot of the north-east forest is just... mysteriously gone.<br /> <br /> This is the North-East now (with the River Province right in the south-east corner there).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/67tcQcvc\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/67tcQcvc/Big-campaign-map.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> So that's how different my Creation is.<br /> <br /> (Sorry the pics are a bit small, but you can click to expand)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T04:16:23-07:00","id":1385232,"title":"","content":"High Wonder is how my Creation differs. I revised the crafting system to try and make artifacts something a skilled mortal artisan could fesibly make, removed the FAA rules, reintroduced Thaumaturgy as teachable arts and have Sorcery more widely available than the default. It's not entirely different everywhere you look - there aren't enough amazing craftsmen everywhere for that to revolutionize the world, but when you reach one of the major Scavenger Lands states, you're likely to run into some impressive stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T16:33:46-07:00","id":1385319,"title":"","content":"Everything takes longer. A society run by people who live for centuries won't implode within 5 years of the Empress vanishing. Downtime of months in a party of Celestials is basically a weekend.<br /> <br /> Also thaumaturgy is a lot more common. Hedge magic of some sort is about as common as left-handedness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T05:07:29-07:00","id":1385800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1379718#post1379718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually Chausse, the reason for that post is that some people think that the Realm has been made much worse in <i>this</i> edition, compared to 2nd ed. I don't really think so (Sesus Chenow's gone, for one thing), but I guess Equitable Remedy does.</div> </div> </div> </div>My charitable take on this is that the cartoonishly evil Dynasts helped to distort the perception of the more honourable ones. If Mnemon is obviously evil and must be stopped you care a lot less about what House V'neef is doing to its Satrapies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T05:54:39-07:00","id":1385806,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, not sure but I could see that maybe. Nellens and most of Sesus looked pretty good by comparison. And I had a friend who thought Cathak Cainan was the bomb, an honourable hero, and I guess compared to Chenow he is.<br /> <br /> Definitely the famous characters I guess are more noticeable than, say, Cathak's brutal tax-extraction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:17:50-07:00","id":1385821,"title":"","content":"It's more that the first two editions tended to fixate on the obvious bad actors and salacious elements.<br /> <br /> For example, if you asked most people who'd read Blood and Salt why the Realm was bad for An-Teng they'd probably start talking about people being forced into a life of sex work even though that's really only a factor in the Shore Lands (it gets two pages!) then once that leap is made, its clearly the work of the more decadent Houses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:45:43-07:00","id":1385832,"title":"","content":"Letting off the less decadent houses (Cathak, Ledaal, etc), you mean?<br /> <br /> Whereas 3rd ed looks at all the Houses and the bad stuff they've done, in a less salacious and thus less distracting way? Or at, giving an overall picture of Empire as inherently problematic, rather than the problems being a few &quot;bad apples&quot; who can be removed? A kind of &quot;if we just banned slavery and the opium trade and the British Empire would be great?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T12:38:43-07:00","id":1385897,"title":"","content":"Precisely that. <br /> There's also an important change that's occurring beyond the Realm, in that more is being done to humanise the proverbial barbarians at the gate so that they're not orcs. Remember how the MoEP: Dragon-Blooded intro comic they used the Varajtul as the enemy Elana was fighting so that the first glimpse some people got of the Realm's enemies was a bunch of monster men who ate people. Something I've found amusing about that in retrospect is that it's highly likely they invaded the \u200bVarajtul's lands rather than the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T14:03:18-07:00","id":1385933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1385897#post1385897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've found amusing about that in retrospect is that it's highly likely they invaded the \u200bVarajtul's lands rather than the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is certainly true, considering the humans who live on that island (and their elkmen buddies) are not a Satrapy.<br /> <br /> Tbh though, I am kind of okay with, say, the Dragonblood book having a comic where the heroic Dragonblood legions fight crazy mutant barbarians, and then another book (Lunars, Compass: North, etc) having a comic where poor innocent mutant barbarians must defend themselves against invading Realm Legions. I'm not too bothered by the Dragonblood book showing things from their point of view, and then show the other point of view elsewhere.<br /> <br /> But then, me and most of my players are British socialists/anarchists/liberals ruled by Bojo and his Empire-loving Tories, so we're never going to read a book that presents colonial aristocrats heroically fighting the (insert racist term about Africans or Indians here), and assume it's something to be taken seriously. Clearly the colonial aristocrats are the bad guys, they just don't <i>realise</i> they're the bad guys because they're hopped up on a self-aggrandising ideology. I guess the writers might worry about some groups not getting that and either being annoyed by Imperial apologism or actually buying into Imperial apologism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T14:59:52-07:00","id":1385947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1385832#post1385832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A kind of &quot;if we just banned slavery and the opium trade and the British Empire would be great?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Somewhat confused ideas then. For the former, it was the only thing that ever did ban slavery and have enough power and range to get it to stick, and for the latter, the War On Drugs hasn't a hard time yielding net harm reduction with modern hard drugs, so it's not so clear what a War On Opium would do with a much more harmless 19th century equivalent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T16:21:12-07:00","id":1385965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1385933#post1385933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the writers might worry about some groups not getting that and either being annoyed by Imperial apologism or actually buying into Imperial apologism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we've got Warhammer 40,000 to point to as an example of what happens if enough people don't get the joke, I've seen it argued before that the big thing which killed the satirical part of the setting was that it didn't translate well to American humour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T16:48:49-07:00","id":1385974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1385965#post1385965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well we've got Warhammer 40,000 to point to as an example of what happens if enough people don't get the joke, I've seen it argued before that the big thing which killed the satirical part of the setting was that it didn't translate well to American humour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly? As a non-American, I couldn't comment on that. But I will say that from 1st ed to 2nd ed to 3rd ed it did look more and more like it took itself seriously. I can why someone who didn't start playing until 4th edition wouldn't pick up on the joke so much. Whereas 1st ed art, Necromunda, etc, makes it somewhat more obvious.<br /> Although they do the Regimental Standard and stuff now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T17:54:31-07:00","id":1385983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1385965#post1385965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well we've got Warhammer 40,000 to point to as an example of what happens if enough people don't get the joke, I've seen it argued before that the big thing which killed the satirical part of the setting was that it didn't translate well to American humour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, people don't think it's funny and they take it too serious, or they don't actually see what's wrong with the Empire of Man?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T03:37:05-07:00","id":1386032,"title":"","content":"Both. They go &quot;ah, the Space Marines are the good guys. This is about how in a world of horrors, with such a huge population there's no choice but to have an authoritarian government that commits war crimes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ah, I remember when our Dark Heresy characters fire-bombed orphanages. Such healthy fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Actually, I was discussing 40k games a bit with a friend after the end of my Rogue Trader game, which, I'll be honest, did not go well. I really enjoyed coming up with the plot, worlds, etc, but... it did not go well. (The group went off-quest in Game 1. In Game 3 half the group tried to abandon the Rogue Trader, but failed and instead took her and half the crew on a small ship with all the astropaths, leaving 2 PCs and the other half the crew on a ship without any fuel and an abandoned desert world where they were stranded for 3 years before joining up again. The ship went through multiple captains, who sometimes shot each other, or used power fists. The Navigator sometimes refused to go anywhere. Once the Rogue Trader put the Tech-Priest and regular Priest in charge of the ship while off on a mission, at which point the Tech-Priest promptly shut down the ship, and then I think the Arch-Militant attempted a coup. Once the Tech-Priest shut down the ship while enemy ships were on their way to shoot them. The game ended with the original Rogue Trader I think dead of space-plague, the Tech-Priest living on one of the three Yu-Vath homeworlds on the wrong side of the Halo Stars, and the Tech-Priest-less and Rogue Trader-less ship with very little fuel about to jump away from a small Yu'vath fleet back across the Halo Stars and hoping they'd get there quickly enough not to run out of fuel and be stranded in the Warp.)<br /> (Ironically, the next game I did with that group of players was Star Wars, where the same players generally worked together really well, I just didn't have any good ideas for plot. I wanted to run something other than Exalted which we play every week, but honestly Lunars is going much better than either of my sci-fi games went.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, he said he thought one issue was that 40k is very much one where different people have different ideas about what it is. Is it about fundamentalist space nazis? Is it a comedy parody of fundamentalist space nazis? A wacky comedy with space goblins? A Brazilia-esque parody of bureaucracy? A serious game of the desperate measures man must take in a hostile universe, and how in the face of Cthulu-demons man must sacrifice liberty and fairness? And when different players have different ideas about what game it is, they clash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T03:42:57-07:00","id":1386034,"title":"","content":"Anyway. I can also see that kind of thing happening with the Realm, with some players being &quot;oh, we're a little morally ambiguous, but basically we're heroes who fight the demons that want to devour the world, like Abyssals and Fae and stuff,&quot; others saying &quot;my character is a monk who wants to help people and protect them,&quot; others thinking &quot;yeah, I'm going to play Julius Caesar/Alexander&quot; and just not thinking about the moral issues, others saying &quot;this is a game about ridiculously decadent aristocrats that 2nd ed said had giant penises, and we have a heroin-pissing dinosaur and take tons of coke with our harem of slave girls,&quot; and then others being &quot;yeah, we're colonial aristocrats and thus my character is an <i>enormous racist</i>* who does not value the lives of Threshold barbarians at all, yes I shall burn down this city because it's ruled by a Solar.&quot; And those may not get on.<br /> <br /> *This one is particularly tricky because a)it's very sensitive, b)people are likely to play this in a rather over-the-top way, but maybe that's actually better than doing it nuanced because if you do it might seem sympathetic, and c)it's kinda realistic, except not quite, because not all prejudice works the same way. But, you know, if your Imperial apologist is a social justice warrior who goes to barbarian societies and teaches them to be more progressive, that really is Imperial apologism the exact way the British ruling class claims?<br /> <br /> I do remember my Russian friend making a joke that &quot;barbarians make great officers when led by Dragonblood&quot; or something like that, and almost getting kicked off the Swansea Roleplaying facebook group for racism.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you probably need to get everyone very broadly on the same page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-06-2020, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T05:24:30-07:00","id":1386045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386034#post1386034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway. I can also see that kind of thing happening with the Realm, with some players being &quot;oh, we're a little morally ambiguous, but basically we're heroes who fight the demons that want to devour the world, like Abyssals and Fae and stuff,&quot; others saying &quot;my character is a monk who wants to help people and protect them,&quot; others thinking &quot;yeah, I'm going to play Julius Caesar/Alexander&quot; and just not thinking about the moral issues, others saying &quot;this is a game about ridiculously decadent aristocrats that 2nd ed said had giant penises, and we have a heroin-pissing dinosaur and take tons of coke with our harem of slave girls,&quot; and then others being &quot;yeah, we're colonial aristocrats and thus my character is an <i>enormous racist</i>* who does not value the lives of Threshold barbarians at all, yes I shall burn down this city because it's ruled by a Solar.&quot; And those may not get on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strive to hit all five.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1385897#post1385897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Precisely that. <br /> There's also an important change that's occurring beyond the Realm, in that more is being done to humanise the proverbial barbarians at the gate so that they're not orcs. Remember how the MoEP: Dragon-Blooded intro comic they used the Varajtul as the enemy Elana was fighting so that the first glimpse some people got of the Realm's enemies was a bunch of monster men who ate people. Something I've found amusing about that in retrospect is that it's highly likely they invaded the \u200bVarajtul's lands rather than the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that's what I like about Exalted.<br /> <br /> The big, classical hero wielding her enormous sword to defend her fallen comrades against cannibals (and escape a loveless marriage)... on the behest of an imperialist, evil empire.<br /> <br /> It's what gives the setting nuance. It's the &quot;but&quot; in &quot;Yes you can topple the Realm, but&quot;.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I like humanizing the barbarians as well. But I don't think it's inappropriate to protagonize a splat in the book pitched at playing that splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-06-2020, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T05:29:20-07:00","id":1386046,"title":"","content":"With your game, or with your character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T05:49:31-07:00","id":1386048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386046#post1386046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With your game, or with your character?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally game.<br /> <br /> Characters can hit notes of all five but seems pretty convoluted to have a pious monk and his heroin dinosaur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-06-2020, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T06:24:31-07:00","id":1386052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386045#post1386045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, that's what I like about Exalted.<br /> <br /> The big, classical hero wielding her enormous sword to defend her fallen comrades against cannibals (and escape a loveless marriage)... on the behest of an imperialist, evil empire.<br /> <br /> It's what gives the setting nuance. It's the &quot;but&quot; in &quot;Yes you can topple the Realm, but&quot;.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I like humanizing the barbarians as well. But I don't think it's inappropriate to protagonize a splat in the book pitched at playing that splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand my issue.<br /> <br /> The portrayal of the barbarians as fanged cannibalistic mutants is in service to The Realm's narrative not Tepet Elena's story. It's still heroic for her to defend wounded soldiers from an enemy who looks like you because getting captured under those circumstances is a &quot;no good can come of this&quot; situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-06-2020, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T06:57:51-07:00","id":1386053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386052#post1386052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You misunderstand my issue.<br /> <br /> The portrayal the barbarians as fanged cannibalistic mutants is in service to The Realm's narrative not Tepet Elena's story. It's still heroic for her to defend wounded soldiers from an enemy who looks like you because getting captured under those circumstances is a &amp;quot;no good can come of this&amp;quot; situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... they are fanged, cannibalistic mutants?<br /> <br /> Like... in 40K the Imperium is a brutal, oppressive, technologically regressive, science hating, witch-burning theocracy... But they fight fanged, cannibalistic mutants.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with a supplement showing that the fanged, cannibalistic mutants have their own culture, art and poetry. I'm fine with a supplement showing that the vast majority of so-called &quot;barbarians&quot; are not fanged, cannibalistic mutants.<br /> <br /> But the Realm really does fight fanged, cannibalistic mutants. And zombie hordes. And armies of nightmares from beyond Creation.<br /> <br /> But the Realm also murders teenage boys who interrupt the opium trade. And the Realm also enslaves, conquers and brutally taxes.<br /> <br /> Tepet Elena heroicly defying orders to protect the fallen from murderous cannibals is a very different story to Tepet Elena deciding that instead of withdrawing she's going to murder some farmers.<br /> <br /> 2E Elena tells PCs, yes the Realm is evil. But look at this Dynast who defied the system to be the hero you could be.<br /> <br /> Killing normal folks defending their home... somewhat takes the shine off that defiance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T07:21:58-07:00","id":1386060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386053#post1386053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tepet Elena heroicly defying orders to protect the fallen from murderous cannibals is a very different story to Tepet Elena deciding that instead of withdrawing she's going to murder some farmers.</div> </div> </div> </div> If the farmers have formed a militia or taken up arms as part of a peasant rebellion they're not going to invite captured enemy soldiers home for family dinner, so defending your comrades from them is still heroic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T07:56:28-07:00","id":1386071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386045#post1386045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't get me wrong, I like humanizing the barbarians as well. But I don't think it's inappropriate to protagonize a splat in the book pitched at playing that splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree with you.<br /> <br /> I like reading these discussions about the world-building of Exalted, but I also feel like if we go too deep into trying to draw direct conclusions about its premises and its biased presentation (&quot;The Realm is like this so it's actually evil&quot; for the simplest example), we are kind of missing the whole point that these are games with the function of allowing you to play certain types of characters who live in their own world. I think it's a mistake to try and make one unique &quot;world-building&quot; out of all the books of Exalted setting in order to draw conclusions about the setting for ludic purpose.<br /> <br /> I think the Solars in the Core Exalted 3e book are not the same Solars in the DB:WFHW books because these books are not here to tell the same story. I think it's fine to play a good imperialist DB that helps people get over their tribalistic way against the barbarian Lunar, just as much I think it's fine to play a heroic Lunar that rises oppressed people against the bad imperialist DB, even while these characters are mechanically the same and act the same inside the story played, but this specific description needs to be put in context of its specific corresponding playbook.<br /> <br /> It doesn't mean you can't tell a story of bad imperialism in DB or of bad rebellion in Lunar or make any subversion of any kind, but I think these subversions need to be made in context of one (or more) playbooks to make sense. <br /> <br /> Trying to tie every aspect of the world into a singular story that can be understood from a single point of view will lead to inevitable contradictions because : <br /> 1) The authors are lying to us. Not on purpose, but the nature of a fictional story is that you can always be proven wrong about any topic if the writer wishes to<br /> 2) We all have a different setting in mind because this is a fictional shared story<br /> 3) This world doesn't work like ours because it doesn't have causality (on any aspect, physical, social, economic, etc ...). It looks it has causality, but it doesn't, because consequences are decided by our human minds, and by nothing else","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:13:27-07:00","id":1386274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386071#post1386071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Solars in the Core Exalted 3e book are not the same Solars in the DB:WFHW books because these books are not here to tell the same story. I think it's fine to play a good imperialist DB that helps people get over their tribalistic way against the barbarian Lunar, just as much I think it's fine to play a heroic Lunar that rises oppressed people against the bad imperialist DB</div> </div> </div> </div>i might agree if the books didn\u2019t exist in a real world social context, and imperialism was as fanciful a concept as Deathknights. But we don\u2019t and it\u2019s not - ergo \u201cgood imperialism\u201d is not a thing. Good people who are part of said system of exploitation and oppression - sure, that\u2019s how systemic evils always work. But there is no context where imperialism becomes a good thing.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not arguing against playing loyal Dynasts here. Just that in that fantasy gaming you\u2019re diegetically implementing systems of oppression and exploitation in this fantasy world. That is the narrative being explored. And I don\u2019t think the books pretend otherwise with regard to what the Dynasts are doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:40:51-07:00","id":1386280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386274#post1386274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i might agree if the books didn\u2019t exist in a real world social context, and imperialism was as fanciful a concept as Deathknights. But we don\u2019t and it\u2019s not - ergo \u201cgood imperialism\u201d is not a thing. Good people who are part of said system of exploitation and oppression - sure, that\u2019s how systemic evils always work. But there is no context where imperialism becomes a good thing.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not arguing against playing loyal Dynasts here. Just that in that fantasy gaming you\u2019re diegetically implementing systems of oppression and exploitation in this fantasy world. That is the narrative being explored. And I don\u2019t think the books pretend otherwise with regard to what the Dynasts are doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to launch into an impassioned defense of what I consider to be one of the greatest evils on Earth... But...<br /> <br /> Exalted does a very poor job of this.<br /> <br /> Whilst both the Realm and the Solar Deliberative are/have been shown as bad, I've yet to see a game that wasn't about the PCs gaining control of their own, Nice Guy(tm) Empire.<br /> <br /> The whole premise of Exalted as that you are playing a returning god-king. And aside from the occasional anarcho-syndicaist complaining that a fiery bint handing out shards of infinite power is no basis for a government, I've never seen a real challenge to the base assumption that the Realm is bad because it wants to kill you, but your empire is totally good because you are a Solar.<br /> <br /> And that said... the British Empire ended Sati and numerous other barbaric customs. It brought technological advancement and (eventually) stamped out slavery. That doesn't change the fact that imperialism is wrong (both in and of itself, and due to the additional evils it perpertrates) but looked at honestly, empires aren't onions: they're always a mix of good and bad. And the Realm is no different.<br /> <br /> If your choices are: an evil empire of elemental super soldiers will save your life but extract taxes; or an evil empire of fanged, mutant cannibals is going to rape you to death, eat your flesh and sow your skin into your clothing (and not necessarily in that order), then I'd be really hesitant to make statements like &quot;there's <b>no</b> context where imperialism becomes a good thing&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sure the Imperium of Man is an outrageous, cartoony, evil that would make Judge Dress blush. Still the good guys in the 40k universe. And Exalted isn't a GrimDark game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-07-2020, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:48:30-07:00","id":1386284,"title":"","content":"It's a whole hell lot more empty of exalts. Exalts are, supposd to be rare. And I write it to be like that. Concentrations of exalts are considered to be world-shaking things, basically the equivalent of a state getting an army, or a nuke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T01:45:25-07:00","id":1386319,"title":"","content":"How rare?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've yet to see a game that wasn't about the PCs gaining control of their own, Nice Guy(tm) Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have. Both in terms of it not being about gaining an Empire, and it not being a Nice Guy Empire. Our Dawn general's concept is Roboute Guilleman/Hitler with a Napoleon complex. In case his Djala Greater Prosperity Zone and ranting about how strength is the greatest good isn't clear enough, not to mention executing Djala who don't subscribe to his fundamentalist monolatrist position, he wears Soulsteel armour with screaming ghost-faces that makes you bow before him.<br /> He also negs the Eclipse.<br /> Although he has slightly<i> improved</i> morally since a different evil monarch killed his friend for disloyalty, and once evil monarchs hurt him personally, he's tried to become a better person. Though not very hard.<br /> <br /> But...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted does a very poor job of this.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've never seen a real challenge to the base assumption that the Realm is bad because it wants to kill you, but your empire is totally good because you are a Solar. </div> </div> </div>I have from groups a lot, I've even used it with NPCs. But the books... well, tbh, I always found 2e's charmset to be subtly deconstructionist, but maybe it was <i>too </i>subtle. And Ex3's lead developers, especially John Morke, were very keen on going in for Solars as the good guys.<br /> So I do somewhat agree with you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your choices are: an evil empire of elemental super soldiers will save your life but extract taxes; or an evil empire of fanged, mutant cannibals is going to rape you to death, eat your flesh and sow your skin into your clothing (and not necessarily in that order), then I'd be really hesitant to make statements like &quot;there's <b>no</b> context where imperialism becomes a good thing&quot;. </div> </div> </div>While I do agree with your overall point, there is the issue that often that is not the only two choices, but Empires believe/present it as your only two choices, or most of all force it as the two choices.<br /> <br /> The most pro-British guy I ever met from our various ex-colonies was a guy from Myanmar. Now, most Burmans have a very negative view of their old colonial overlords, but he was from an isolated hill tribe in the north-west mountains. He told me all about this British missionary who'd come to his village and taught them modern medicine, how to read (they had no alphabet for their language, so he made them one based on Burman which obviously benefited them later in learning Myanmar's largest language), and that Jesus loves you but is <i>not cool</i> with cutting off people's heads to decorate your village.<br /> So for this tribe, the British were great... except it wasn't really the British <i>Empire</i>, whose policy towards the hill tribes was to mostly just occasionally ride around waving flags and saying &quot;we're in charge, check out how awesome we are&quot; and then go home, whereas the low landers were fully conquered with the whole &quot;pay tax or get shot&quot; policy. Spreading modern medicine, etc doesn't actually require conquering people. (And I think it's interesting that many of Myanmar's hill tribes are Christian or semi-Christian, whereas Burmans are mostly Buddhist; we British were far more successful at religious conversion in areas that were not under brutal occupation. I wonder why? I almost suspect it might be somewhat similar to why most Welsh people under the Empire were Protestant, and most Irish were not.)*<br /> <br /> <br /> With 40K, the Imperium protects humanity from Orcs, Chaos, etc, but it's honestly not that great. It's riven with corruption, elitism, feudalism, etc, that severely impacts humanity's production levels, not to mention encourages people to rebel, turn to Chaos, change sides and join the Tau, etc, etc. The Imperium of man isn't so much a matter of &quot;we must make great sacrifices to defend humanity&quot; as &quot;it's impossible for twelve AI-hating humans to functionally administer a galactic empire without reliable FTL travel or a unified technological base&quot;. It's &quot;Was China's response to Coronavirus good?&quot; And the answer is sort of yes, because they can do whatever it takes to crush it, but it wouldn't have been such a problem if it wasn't a paranoid authoritarian state in the first place.<br /> <br /> There's also the issue that the Imperium's violent xenophobia is a self-defeating prophecy; aliens hate us so we hate them so they hate us so we hate them. War against the Necrons or Tyranids is necessary, not necessarily the Craftworlds or Tau or Zoats or whatever.<br /> <br /> I honestly wonder if the whole &quot;Roboute Guilleman is back and he's not so keen on what the Imperium's become&quot; is that the writers gave up on trying to present the Imperium as a parody, and were just like &quot;sigh, we'll make half the galaxy the kind of good Imperium, and half can be the grimdark one for the grognards to play in.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> *So back to the Realm. I have seen sometimes good plot with the tension between the Immaculate Monks who want to educate the locals, heal them, save them from corrupt gods and ravenous Raksha, and destroy their local culture and beliefs**, and the nobles who want to find ways to tax the locals dry but honestly don't care about the local religion that much and are cool with them keeping their own culture, and may even quite enjoy that culture, ala East India Company men. You can also do tensions like the early colonial slave-owners who wouldn't let their slaves learn about Christianity because then they wouldn't be able to justify enslaving them.<br /> <br /> **Though you can also do tensions between the monks who are happy to syncretise stuff and the ones who aren't. Obviously Pure Way/Realm Immaculates are the obvious one here, but I think you can quite happily do it with just Immaculates.<br /> This may be the kind of thing some in my group enjoy, but not others though?<br /> <br /> Anyway. John, I do agree with your point that of course few (maybe not 0) real-world governments are 100% bad, and that even includes Empires, especially ones who believe in their own &quot;civilising mission&quot; which the Realm very much does. But then, Empire vs Anarchy or Empire vs Conquest By Worse People are often (not always!*** But often) a false dichotomy.<br /> <br /> And this can be a difficult thing to present clearly. Exalted's not great at it, but I guess it does somewhat try. I think some people would like it to not try, and I don't think that's the answer, because if nothing else it's dull.<br /> <br /> ***David Ben-Gurion and Aang San are both examples of nationalist leaders who switched back and forth between opposing and supporting the British and other Empires, not because they liked the British, but in a world of clashing huge Empires yeah, sometimes you have no alternative.<br /> That doesn't mean we British didn't have an alternative to being dicks of course (and in both cases we eventually f***ed off, though not completely because we thought it was the moral thing to leave), it's just that we didn't leave the locals with much alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-07-2020, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T02:42:26-07:00","id":1386334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386274#post1386274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i might agree if the books didn\u2019t exist in a real world social context, and imperialism was as fanciful a concept as Deathknights. But we don\u2019t and it\u2019s not - ergo \u201cgood imperialism\u201d is not a thing. Good people who are part of said system of exploitation and oppression - sure, that\u2019s how systemic evils always work. But there is no context where imperialism becomes a good thing.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not arguing against playing loyal Dynasts here. Just that in that fantasy gaming you\u2019re diegetically implementing systems of oppression and exploitation in this fantasy world. That is the narrative being explored. And I don\u2019t think the books pretend otherwise with regard to what the Dynasts are doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, as I said, if Exalted was a series of books or an essay about the evolution of customs in civilizations I'd agree with you, but it's not only that. It's also an interactive commercial medium to play out a whole kind of pseudo-Eastern fantasy tropes.<br /> <br /> I won't be the one arguing that imperialism is good in this forum (because I'm not crazy enough to do that, and because I don't think that), but I also want to argue with people that try to do an analysis of the Exalted setting solely from a moralistic and historical point of view, as if Exalted was an objective history book, then they are missing a part of what is Exalted as a roleplaying game.<br /> <br /> I think it's a better place to approach splats books not only as a part of the greater whole Exalted setting, but also as its own independent perspective on what the world is and why it should be that way, and accept that they can propose experiences that go outside our cultural scope and what our history has taught us about our own actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 05-07-2020, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:41:52-07:00","id":1386368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386280#post1386280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your choices are: an evil empire of elemental super soldiers will save your life but extract taxes; or an evil empire of fanged, mutant cannibals is going to rape you to death, eat your flesh and sow your skin into your clothing (and not necessarily in that order), then I'd be really hesitant to make statements like &quot;there's <b>no</b> context where imperialism becomes a good thing&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is my problem. In this scenario the empire of fanged, mutant cannibals <i>exists</i> for the sole purpose of justifying imperialism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:55:50-07:00","id":1386373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386368#post1386368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is my problem. In this scenario the empire of fanged, mutant cannibals <i>exists</i> for the sole purpose of justifying imperialism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. The Varajtul exist to give PC Lunars a glance at who they might recruit as allies to crush the Realm (since their introduction in The Lunars in 1E). They're about mystic divination and the alternative spirituality of the Wyld. <br /> <br /> The fact that the Realm only sees them as fanged, cannibalistic monsters is incidental to who they are and what they're for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T06:17:09-07:00","id":1386376,"title":"","content":"You're not really talking about the Varajtul though, you're literally talking about an expy of the Reavers.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T06:21:01-07:00","id":1386378,"title":"","content":"I didn't read their description in 1st ed, but in 2nd ed they were descendants of a beautful artistic foodie city (so a tragedy of a fallen kingdom rather than a move from urban to healthier rural living or some such), are described as &quot;savage&quot; or &quot;monstrous&quot; almost every time they're mentioned, do not talk to non-Varajtul, do not consider non-Varajtul people, have a religion that encourages them to attack peaceful innocents and eat them, or even better, take them to a Wyld pocket, dissect them with a blade of unmelting ice, and eat them alive. Their ghosts form the Empire of Hunger, and those who were ritually eaten by the Varajtul are bound in mystic slavery for all time (assuming they're lucky enough not to get moliated into a tree, chair, piece of art, etc). While the White-furred Ghosts don't live with the Black-furred Ghosts (spectres and mortwrights), they get on okay with them, and are currently in negotiations.<br /> <br /> Every time Varajtul are mentioned in one of the other culture's societies, it's as the archetypal threat that all north-westerners must fear, doing whatever it takes to protect themselves from the Varajtul.<br /> <br /> That's not one writer either, that's across 3 or 4 books.<br /> <br /> I'm totally fine with cool furry four-armed cannibals who are about mystic divination and alternative spirituality, but 2nd ed presents them as The Bad Guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T06:30:22-07:00","id":1386379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386378#post1386378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't read their description in 1st ed, but in 2nd ed they were descendants of a beautful artistic foodie city (so a tragedy of a fallen kingdom rather than a move from urban to healthier rural living or some such), are described as &quot;savage&quot; or &quot;monstrous&quot; almost every time they're mentioned, do not talk to non-Varajtul, do not consider non-Varajtul people, have a religion that encourages them to attack peaceful innocents and eat them, or even better, take them to a Wyld pocket, dissect them with a blade of unmelting ice, and eat them alive. Their ghosts form the Empire of Hunger, and those who were ritually eaten by the Varajtul are bound in mystic slavery for all time (assuming they're lucky enough not to get moliated into a tree, chair, piece of art, etc). While the White-furred Ghosts don't live with the Black-furred Ghosts (spectres and mortwrights), they get on okay with them, and are currently in negotiations.<br /> <br /> Every time Varajtul are mentioned in one of the other culture's societies, it's as the archetypal threat that all north-westerners must fear, doing whatever it takes to protect themselves from the Varajtul.<br /> <br /> That's not one writer either, that's across 3 or 4 books.<br /> <br /> I'm totally fine with cool furry four-armed cannibals who are about mystic divination and alternative spirituality, but 2nd ed presents them as The Bad Guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard even worse. <br /> <br /> Some people say that ... <span style=\"font-size:8px\">they put pineapple on </span><span style=\"font-size:8px\">pizzas </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">I'm still having nightmares.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T06:38:48-07:00","id":1386380,"title":"","content":"That seems unlikely.<br /> <br /> The book says the &quot;Varajtul's opinions about cuisine are... interesting.&quot;<br /> <br /> Eating humans isn't healthy (prions), not to mention the whole murder issue, but is at least interesting. (Played a cannibal Dragonblood once.)<br /> Pineapple on pizza may be bad, but it is also not interesting.<br /> <br /> The Varajtul may be monsters, but when it comes to food they do have standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T06:46:19-07:00","id":1386384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386378#post1386378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't read their description in 1st ed, but in 2nd ed they were descendants of a beautful artistic foodie city (so a tragedy of a fallen kingdom rather than a move from urban to healthier rural living or some such), are described as &quot;savage&quot; or &quot;monstrous&quot; almost every time they're mentioned, do not talk to non-Varajtul, do not consider non-Varajtul people, have a religion that encourages them to attack peaceful innocents and eat them, or even better, take them to a Wyld pocket, dissect them with a blade of unmelting ice, and eat them alive. Their ghosts form the Empire of Hunger, and those who were ritually eaten by the Varajtul are bound in mystic slavery for all time (assuming they're lucky enough not to get moliated into a tree, chair, piece of art, etc). While the White-furred Ghosts don't live with the Black-furred Ghosts (spectres and mortwrights), they get on okay with them, and are currently in negotiations.<br /> <br /> Every time Varajtul are mentioned in one of the other culture's societies, it's as the archetypal threat that all north-westerners must fear, doing whatever it takes to protect themselves from the Varajtul.<br /> <br /> That's not one writer either, that's across 3 or 4 books.<br /> <br /> I'm totally fine with cool furry four-armed cannibals who are about mystic divination and alternative spirituality, but 2nd ed presents them as The Bad Guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I retract my previous statement, in that Doe was literally quoting Serenity and talking about the Reavers not the Varajtul but I don't consider the distinction important enough in the context of 1st and 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> I still consider the portrayal of the Varajtul and similar groups as echoing racist beliefs concerning indigenous populations, enabling a white man's burden narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-07-2020, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T06:49:47-07:00","id":1386386,"title":"","content":"Didn't the evil Imperialists in Firefly actualy create the cannibal-rapists who sew clothes out of human skin though, and basically refuse to fight them?<br /> <br /> I've watched all of Firefly a few times, but I think I only watched Serenity once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T07:59:32-07:00","id":1386403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386386#post1386386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't the evil Imperialists in Firefly actualy create the cannibal-rapists who sew clothes out of human skin though, and basically refuse to fight them?<br /> <br /> I've watched all of Firefly a few times, but I think I only watched Serenity once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> The obvious Bad Guy Barbarians and &quot;obvious&quot; Good Guy Empire gets hella turned on its head in Serenity. The Alliance is exactly where I like my Realm. Happy Unity Day.<br /> <br /> And technically, The Battle of Five Fangs is supposed to be in response to the Varajtul attacking a client state of the Realm... But we all suspect* the Realm started it.<br /> <br /> *know <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386384#post1386384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still consider the portrayal of the Varajtul and similar groups as echoing racist beliefs concerning indigenous populations, enabling a white man's burden narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, not least because the Realm is dominated by the Wan. Nor do I consider a white man's burden narrative inherently problematic for a story, especially if placed within a culturally sensitive arc about growth and understanding. I'd go further to say, that some cultures do practice cannibalism: yes, baseless accusations of cannibalism have been used by imperialistic conquerors to dehumanize and other &quot;barbarians&quot;, but people <i>do </i>eat people. More than that, we're talking about fantastic people mutated by magic powers, not exactly an obvious stand-in for a real life ethinic group facing persecution. And, again, there are protagonistic aspects to the Varajtul, who are heroic in their default presentation but presented in a different light in an opposing splat book. I would not want to play Exalted if every faction had to be unambiguously less evil than the Realm.<br /> <br /> But, I think it's important to respect the opinions and feelings of the players involved, and I acknowledge that it makes you uncomfortable to have the Varajtul prominently displayed in the setting as cannibal barbarians kept in check by the Realm (as I acknowledge the history of colonial racism which informs your discomfort).<br /> <br /> I still think, however, that &quot;Exalted against the Wyld&quot; is an appropriate narrative space for a Dragon-Blooded hero in general, and that Tepet Elena's narrative is a lot less heroic if she fighting against normal mortals, specifically. I'm explicitly fine with the Realm fighting against worse evils than itself, because that adds a layer of moral complication and consequence for the PCs to engage with. In order for the Realm to fight against such evils, these evils must exist. I don't see the Varajtul as lionizing the Realm as much as I see them as an obstacle the PCs have to deal with if they topple the Realm (or people they can use to topple the Realm). And they're an appropriate foil for Dynast PCs -- the Realm wanted Tepet Elena to feed her wounded soldiers to the cannibals, that's not exactly casting the Realm in a positive light. When she relates the story in MoEP: DB it's a story about how she disobeyed the Realm once and is prepared to disobey the Realm again, it's not a story about how awesome the Empire is at conquering savages.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's my piece. If you want to have the last word, feel free but I'm not going to post further on this because I don't want to derail the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-07-2020, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T13:30:08-07:00","id":1386470,"title":"","content":"On the comic:<br /> I think someone can impart more than one meaning from a piece of art. <br /> For some people the comic was their first real impression of the Realm in which they're depicted fighting literal monsters. I also don't agree that Elena ever disobeys 'the Realm' just a cowardly officer and now her selfish parents in order to continue her duties as a magistrate and enforce the Empress' laws. <br /> <br /> On Cannibalism:<br /> Most societies that practiced cannibalism did something much more akin to how the Lintha eat their dead. I've never heard of anything like the Varajtul outside of serial killers. There's debate among anthropologists if cannibalism has ever been 100% socially acceptable among humans, anywhere ever. <br /> <br /> On the point I was making two pages ago:<br /> I never saw the Realm of previous editions as pro-Imperialism because I'm a pretty serious student of History. So, much as I'm looking at possible shortcomings in the presentation of previous editions (especially 2nd edition) that could've led people to the wrong conclusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:23:29-07:00","id":1386489,"title":"","content":"This is not the place and I'm not the person for another tangent on assessment of empires' legacies in our world, but... Creation is a poor world if you're interested in the hoary old trope of &quot;Our people lived in fellowship and peace, under the guidance of the wise elders we all chose to lead us... until The Empire came, with its fire, steel, division and exploitation. So I and my band resist them, first in secret, then openly.&quot;. <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure there are carve-outs for that in the setting (some of the East) and you can invent places for which that's true, but for the most part it's a Time of Tumult in a world with a lot up for grabs, with lots of peoples on the move, Scavenger Lords setting themselves up as autocrats, etc. The Lintha Family and The Perfect and such are just about, y'know, and if the Realm offers you a handshake of alliance in a mailed glove, it's not always the worst deal.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's true before we even get to the &quot;monsters&quot; that don't exist our world and can justify empire building of both the Solar sort (and which are base facets of the world; there are always gonna be hobgoblins, undead etc). <br /> <br /> To some extent maybe 3e core tries to dial this a little differently (I can't speak on the DB book), but it's fundamentally not this kind of Hawkmoon-y world with &quot;the one evil empire&quot; and that's not really what the most core stuff was trying to do (the Realm is fundamentally built to be bad enough that it's worth the Solars fighting, but not bad enough that Dynasts don't regard it as worth defending, and as a bonus, a commentary on why Grabowski thought autocracy sucked, and it has limits to bearing too much more weight than that). So there's a limit to that.<br /> <br /> <br /> (It's thankfully equally a poor place for the most part for cultures which are *forced* to be cartoonishly evil to survive).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T18:11:03-07:00","id":1386573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386403#post1386403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree, not least because the Realm is dominated by the Wan.</div> </div> </div> </div>To say that the Realm is not informed by examples and outlooks arising from the modern history of Western Europe because they don't resemble them physically is pretty superficial, not least because the Wan/the Realm has still largely been written by white people of Western European cultural descent.<br /> <br /> Like, not just the imperialism; the Immaculate Order's system of religious supremacy, establishment and absolutism and the manner in which it is used to provide a moral justification for imperialism has a lot more in common with English Protestantism than it does with any Asian religion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nor do I consider a white man's burden narrative inherently problematic for a story, especially if placed within a culturally sensitive arc about growth and understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>That arc is more difficult to accomplish when presented with an antagonist that is reduced down to a horrific monster people who lack apparent semblance of a sophisticated inner life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go further to say, that some cultures do practice cannibalism: yes, baseless accusations of cannibalism have been used by imperialistic conquerors to dehumanize and other &quot;barbarians&quot;, but people <i>do </i>eat people.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what?<br /> <br /> I'll point out that there's a distinct difference between the historical example of &quot;consumption of flesh is an aspect of already existing practices of warfare&quot; and the fictional trope of depicting a culture that sets out to make war on people for the specific purpose of eating them.<br /> <br /> And sure, there can be a certain cultural weight to a marauding army engaging in cannibalism or alternative desecrations of the bodies of the dead for purposes of humiliation, although it has its most deviant character when the ones doing the humiliation are the aggressors who possess a disproportionate amount of power and have undertaken war for the sake of profit or indulgence of some base violent need. I think there are key differences between the Brussians going in to roll over the Krukanians at the behest of their authoritarian president and cannibalising enemy soldiers as a tactic of terror and humiliation than if the resisting and less powerful force engaged in such a desecration as part of a message of &quot;fuck off and leave us alone&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the Brussians then turn around and have the state press try to both sides it, or worse retroactively state &quot;look, the violent extremes they engage in while resisting us serve as a post hoc justification for our annexation in the first place&quot;, they're disingenuously trying to control the narrative by presenting key elements out of context, and it lacks a certain sophistication to take that narrative at face value.<br /> <br /> That being said, there's a stronger degree of narrative and historical value to the point that empires or other forms of centralised authority have used the actual fact of border communities being at risk from raiders to justify greater degrees of power, and there are ways to portray that in terms of &quot;complex circumstances can make people accept bad systems with the best of intentions&quot; that manage to dance below the threshold of &quot;external raiders justify imperialism&quot;. Not least by having a mind for the fact that the raiders have historically been actual people with material concerns that strongly inform their raiding culture (while also not forming the entirety of it; within such a society, there's always a point at which people within such a society go beyond raiding as material necessity and into the level of personal aggrandizement).<br /> <br /> While keeping in mind that we've got historical examples of those forms of border raiding giving way to mutually beneficial arrangements driven by interpersonal familiarity, cultural exchange and diplomatic overtures, something that is only possible when both parties recognise one another's inherent humanity (that they also have to possess).<br /> <br /> That's a very shaky dance to engage in, I expect even the best writers to fumble a few of the steps. Good faith artistic discourse can point out those fumbles while recognising the good intent and not condemning the work as a whole, as well as being able to acknowledge those imperfections without feeling attacked or otherwise losing one's mind. Or even like... yeah, sometimes people will react to it strongly enough to actually attack somebody, and there's a maturity to being able to weather some of those attacks, even point out their mistakes, without doing something like angrily doubling down and refusing to make any shifts.<br /> <br /> And yes, there are fantastical stories that do want to sometimes just utilise the compelling aesthetic elements of something like a militaristic society or grandiose empire, or even just... war in general without wanting to grapple with the problematic moral dimensions of such, and so create an opponent that is unrelentingly violent and cannot be reasoned with. That kind of fiction can even be enjoyed, although it ought to be mindful of the degree to which it resembles propaganda narratives, because otherwise it still functions as a form of propaganda.<br /> <br /> That's the thing about propaganda, it's not really about making a rational argument, it's about forming psychological habits. Most people are not so compartmentalized that they can readily separate the emotional centres that process fiction from the world view that engages with reality, and that does mean that the mental processes of &quot;the enemy can be something sufficiently inhuman that the only recourse is to destroy it&quot; is something that can more readily be applied to the real world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">More than that, we're talking about fantastic people mutated by magic powers, not exactly an obvious stand-in for a real life ethinic group facing persecution.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a Thermian Argument. The fantastic people don't exist as a result of independent processes, they were created by a writer, and artistic critique interrogates both why they opted to write that thing and what kinds of reactions it creates in people. All art is political.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, again, there are protagonistic aspects to the Varajtul, who are heroic in their default presentation but presented in a different light in an opposing splat book. I would not want to play Exalted if every faction had to be unambiguously less evil than the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question of whether any given community or organisation is more or less &quot;evil&quot; than the Realm is a complicated one, particularly considering that the Realm has no opponent that is in possession of greater reach or resources than them, but it's still possible to thread the needle of portraying local instances of the Realm fighting an enemy that engages in genuinely grotesque actions without lending anything to the framing of &quot;and the existence of such greater threats ultimately justifies the Realm's existence and provides allowances for its excesses&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's possible to present that scenario and avoid that framing <i>even while depicting the people under Realm rule as believing that their protection justifies their oppression</i>.<br /> <br /> Feedback from the audience helps calibrate that portrayal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think, however, that &quot;Exalted against the Wyld&quot; is an appropriate narrative space for a Dragon-Blooded hero in general, and that Tepet Elena's narrative is a lot less heroic if she fighting against normal mortals, specifically. I'm explicitly fine with the Realm fighting against worse evils than itself, because that adds a layer of moral complication and consequence for the PCs to engage with. In order for the Realm to fight against such evils, these evils must exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of... half agree with this. How do I put it...<br /> <br /> Alexander the Great is a figure who, in his personality and audacity and accomplishments, is truly impressive and compelling... while also being an absolute prick at best and a genuine monster at worst. Like, as a warrior and general he was truly brave and intelligent and lucky and charismatic and exceptionally strong and hardy, who not only commanded intricate campaigns and elaborate battles but personally threw himself into the thick of fighting and took wounds of a kind you would expect to be life ending today <i>repeatedly</i>. While also being somebody who undertook great campaigns of conquest that resulted in the deaths of huge numbers of people out of a belief in himself as a man of destiny and general desire to elevate himself and indulge in that thrill of battle, was paranoid and impulsive and violent in a manner that resulted in the horrible and arbitrary deaths of people in his close personal circle even when they'd displayed incredible loyalty to him, and there's a strong case to be made for him having deliberately led his army back through a hellish desert march resulting in much suffering and death after they refused to continue campaigning into India.<br /> <br /> Taken as a personage, even the things that make him a terrible person make him a compelling figure to look at the life story of.<br /> <br /> And there's an emotional need that can be engaged through the safe medium of fiction in which a person like and scenarios such as that, which would realistically be... let's say exhausting to deal with, can have interaction from a position of safety and freedom from consequence. In those terms, I argue that it is possible to engage with what is compelling in somebody like a Realm political leader or soldier or general <i>without</i> giving them a greater evil in comparison. I quite like this Edition's portrayal of Mnemon exactly as she is, warts and all. She requires no (objective, external) justification. Indeed, I would find leaning too heavily on a point of &quot;if Mnemon doesn't take the throne and beat all competing factions into line, then the Realm is almost certainly going to fall and leave the world exposed to even greater evils&quot; to actually <i>diminish</i> what is compelling about her.<br /> <br /> It takes a certain kind of writing and a certain kind of audience to engage with the narrative of what was compelling about the life of Alexander the Great without falling into the trap of being enamoured with him in a manner that <i>does</i> have real life consequences. Which do exist; now more than any other period in my lifetime, we have examples of people who want to appeal to the base urge of what makes Alexander compelling to accumulate their own power while also illustrating how so many people giving into that urge and provide that power is more likely to lead to disaster. Statistically, we're so much more likely to get somebody who sells the paper mask of a strongman that is incompetent (and likely malicious) in the face of genuine crisis.<br /> <br /> And as I said above, that kind of fiction writing, and even engagement, will probably never be 100%. It takes participation in conversations such as this (and preferably a bit of reading into some actual history books or political and philosophical treatises and a decent amount of journalism) to make up the difference. Talking to people with a broad array of experiences and perspectives and learning more about the world is the kind of thing that, say, prevents a person from falling into the trap of thinking that China's models of state capitalism and international agenda are actually kind of a good thing (a mask being set up a bit by film media that gratifyingly depicts Chinese authorities as reasonable, intelligent and diligent), and can be taken as separated from the severe political and ethnic repression and political culture of secretive elitism.<br /> <br /> However, my final word on things as Exalted goes is... the foundations of Exalted and the manner in which it initially portrays itself are ones in which it wants to ultimately challenge the kinds of power narrative that rationalize the existence of the Realm. The cannibals, the demons, the Wyld, those all come later, and...<br /> <br /> Shit, I was ready to say that presenting them in those terms of &quot;indulge in the fantasy of the enemy that cannot be reasoned with&quot; is incongruous with the core elements, and I still kind of think that's the case to a strong degree, but I'm also suddenly struck by the notion that part of the value of a large, multifaceted setting and premise conveyed with multiple source books is that it can support a variety of narrative approaches in different people's games, as determined by which books they give the greatest focus to. Okay, I have to admit, I was outmanoeuvred on that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-07-2020, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T02:29:21-07:00","id":1386650,"title":"","content":"So there's various things I could say to agree or disagree with various people, but I wonder if this discussion has developed in sufficient directions, with enough points made or considered, to leave it and get back to the main thread topic? What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-08-2020, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T02:37:06-07:00","id":1386653,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>, I don't really know that the Immaculate Philosophy has many parallels to Protestantism, or more specifically English Protestantism, particularly. It seems:<br /> <br /> \u200bHindu/Buddhist - hierarchical reincarnation towards more perfect and more enlightened forms.<br /> <br /> Lamaist/Theravada/Catholic - in its overarching religious structure, parallel to a secular structure and not exactly co-terminous with it, and serving as a source of moral authority for secular structure and check on behaviour of the nobility (and ofen allies with the people in opposition to the state to do so).<br /> <br /> Confucian - in the emphasis on a precisely ordered and hierarchical set of &quot;proper&quot; behaviours for persons of different social status, mandated ultimately by Heaven, and ultimately in service of preserving social order (the proper order of relationships) and the rule of the sovereign as a high good.<br /> <br /> The status of the Immaculate Dragons also seems rather generally Buddhist and to a lesser extent generically Christian (perfected, incarnated individuals in the past who set teachings for people today and were involved in some sort of ritual self-sacrifice against sin and evil, for the greater good of humanity).<br /> <br /> It's a kind of fake engineered religion in setting, so what it does is not really like a real religion - there's no such religion that actually goes &quot;By unholding the orders, stability and social standing of the state and your social superiors, you gain merit for your next incarnation&quot;, which is a kind of too much of an &quot;evil fantasy state church&quot; thing to be quite true. But I think it's built most strongly on a base of engaging with most Asian religious traditions and trying to use those to shape its setting, and is &quot;about&quot; them, in a sense (it's not a Eurocentric rehearsing of European theological disputes dressed up with an Asian gloss, but is genuinely engaging with those ideas).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T05:07:28-07:00","id":1386660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386653#post1386653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, I don't really know that the Immaculate Philosophy has many parallels to Protestantism, or more specifically English Protestantism, particularly.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did I say specifically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T06:20:17-07:00","id":1386669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386660#post1386660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What did I say specifically?</div> </div> </div> </div>This: <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Like, not just the imperialism; the Immaculate Order's system of religious supremacy, establishment and absolutism and the manner in which it is used to provide a moral justification for imperialism has a lot more in common with English Protestantism than it does with any Asian religion.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T06:26:27-07:00","id":1386672,"title":"","content":"So I'm asking you to unpack it a bit more as to why you think that's more applicable than in &quot;any Asian religion&quot;, or indeed any European religion, or any religion. Why is it more applicable than in Theravada Buddhism in SE Asia, or in Catholic conquest in the Baltic and South America, and so forth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T06:37:45-07:00","id":1386673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386672#post1386672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm asking you to unpack it a bit more as to why you think that's more applicable than in &quot;any Asian religion&quot;, or indeed any European religion, or any religion. Why is it more applicable than in Theravada Buddhism in SE Asia, or in Catholic conquest in the Baltic and South America, and so forth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Who are you referring to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T06:49:10-07:00","id":1386675,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a>, the person I'm originally talking to, not yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T06:59:25-07:00","id":1386678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386675#post1386675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a>, the person I'm originally talking to, not yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, I apologise. I thought you were a 3rd party outside Isator and Levi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T08:12:38-07:00","id":1386976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386672#post1386672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm asking you to unpack it a bit more as to why you think that's more applicable than in &amp;quot;any Asian religion&amp;quot;, or indeed any European religion, or any religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a start, because it's an element of my cultural background; I was brought up learning about English religious persecution in Ireland.<br /> <br /> But expanding from that, the degree to which England drove all other religions underground stands out to me just that little bit more from the manner in which they persecuted even their own offshoots of Anglicanism. That's the major thing, the manner in which the Immaculate Philosophy is the only permissable religion, more than its specific theology.<br /> <br /> Mind, there's also the fact that Anglicanism is entwined with its state to a degree that stands out even among European religions. The monarch is still head of the church, and as the monarch is &quot;advised&quot; by the prime minister clerical appointments are a religious topic. Bishops remain prominent peers in the House of Lords, and I'm familiar with the history of when that meant something. That resonates with the kind of authority the Order has, where it sanctions and is sanctioned by the state.<br /> <br /> And the manner in which it was incorporated into the colonialism stands out because, in addition to the local examples, there's just <i>so much</i> of it that the British dotted around the world.<br /> <br /> Plus the way that I find the Perfected Hierarchy to feel kind of like dharma by way of Protestant Work Ethic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it more applicable than in Theravada Buddhism in SE Asia</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I'm not sufficiently familiar with the history of Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar, Sri Lanka or Thailand to make a judgement one way or the other about how they dealt with religious plurality. My reference point is the history of religion in India and China.<br /> <br /> Of course, one reason that it would be more applicable from where I'm standing is that Burma never went and took over England and started forcing Anglican churches to adopt Buddhist clerical practices. That is the part that stands out to me about the Immaculate Order, at least in terms of a discussion of how the cultural background of the writers informs the writing of the Realm, and background of the majority of the audience informs its reading.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">or in Catholic conquest in the Baltic and South America, and so forth?</div> </div> </div> </div>The things I stated before about the manner in which it is institutionalised have some of the subtle details that make the difference to me, but it's not proscriptive. If you're going to include references to other European religions in relation to colonialism, I'm not exactly going to find it to dispute my point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T11:05:57-07:00","id":1387017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1386976#post1386976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a start, because it's an element of my cultural background; I was brought up learning about English religious persecution in Ireland.<br /> <br /> But expanding from that, the degree to which England drove all other religions underground stands out to me just that little bit more from the manner in which they persecuted even their own offshoots of Anglicanism. That's the major thing, the manner in which the Immaculate Philosophy is the only permissable religion, more than its specific theology.<br /> <br /> Mind, there's also the fact that Anglicanism is entwined with its state to a degree that stands out even among European religions. The monarch is still head of the church, and as the monarch is &quot;advised&quot; by the prime minister clerical appointments are a religious topic. Bishops remain prominent peers in the House of Lords, and I'm familiar with the history of when that meant something. That resonates with the kind of authority the Order has, where it sanctions and is sanctioned by the state.<br /> <br /> And the manner in which it was incorporated into the colonialism stands out because, in addition to the local examples, there's just <i>so much</i> of it that the British dotted around the world.<br /> <br /> Plus the way that I find the Perfected Hierarchy to feel kind of like dharma by way of Protestant Work Ethic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some observations: you seem to be suggesting that this is the lens through which to view the Immaculate Order and the Realm, because the US is sufficiently drenched with the influence of Anglicanism to the extent that it can't help but be the lens through which US authors would view it. This strikes me as implausible for a variety of reasons, particularly the different relation of Church and State in the US, where most players and authors of Exalted will be from.<br /> <br /> It's true that the British empire (and 19th century imperialism in general) *is* an influence on aspects of the Realm and its imperialism in some ways (but not others [1]), but it's also the case that the original setting developer claims to have taken the relationship between Buddhism and the state in Imperial China as his model for the relationship between the Immaculate Philosophy and the state. There is *plenty* of precedent for suppression of rival sects by the politically dominant, state supported sect in Chinese history -- a good summary of this happening during the Tang can be found in the chapter on religion in Lewis' <b>China's Cosmopolitan Empire</b>, for instance. Another important dysanalogy between Anglicanism and the IP would be that the Empress is not the head of the order in the same way the monarch is the supreme governer of the Church of England and the Church of Scotland [2, 3]; , which is again closer to the case of the relationship between Imperial throne and a powerful sect in China or (I assume) to the relationship between the Catholic Church and the monarchy in the Spanish and Portugese Empires (aka the reason why there are a lot of Roman Catholics in South America).<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that you're wrong that it's a lens through which to view the Realm and the IP -- it clearly<i> can </i>shed some useful light on it (but then, so can Roman and Persian imperialism) -- but the authoritative way you state it as if it were<i> the </i>primary lens through which everyone else should view it just seems off to me, especially in that it seems to place some fairly specific aspects of the history of the British Isles at the centre of the influences on these texts and their interpretation that the authors might reasonably be expected to know very little about.<br /> <br /> Also, some general points about Anglicanism: While much of what you say about the political structure of Anglicanism is probably fair enough when talking about the period between Henry VIII wanting to get his divorce on and the end of the 19th century, it's really not true in the way you make out anymore. To begin with, the state church in Scotland is Presbytarian, not Anglican (Scottish Anglicanism is represented by the Scottish Episcopalians from whom US Episcopalians are descended); neither the Church of Ireland or Church in Wales (both disestablished, one in the late 19th century and one in the 20th) regard the monarch as their Supreme Governer, nor does any province of the Church outside of England (though the Queen is a Canon of the Cathedral of St Davids, which if it weren't a meaningless honourary title would just mean that she's technically subordinate to the local bishop). It's also worth noting the contributions of Welsh and Scottish non-Anglican Protestant missionaries to the imperial project in addition to those of Anglican missionaries (this was a big thing in 19thC Welsh nationalism, for instance), but also that Catholic and Eastern Orthodox empires were prone to exporting religion in a similar fashion. While the presence of (English) Bishops in the House of Lords is a constitutional anomaly worth fixing, you could argue that the Church of England is entangled with the state to far less an extent than the Lutheran Churches in Scandinavia were until comparatively recently, where clergy were direct employees of the state and church buildings were state property, neither or which are the case in the UK [4]. (In fact, legally clergy aren't even employees under UK law.)<br /> <br /> The Protestant Work Ethic (to the extent that it exists at all as a thing) strikes me as more a non-Conformist or at best Low Church Anglican thing rather than describing the denomination as a whole (there exist a whole bunch of Anglicans who dislike being called Protestants, as they regard themselves as more Catholic than the Pope), but I'm willing to be corrected on that.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, the Anglican Church has a pretty awful history that it needs to account for, but it's one that's bad enough by itself without any need for overstatement.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [1] One dysanalogy would be that the Realm doesn't seem to do settler colonialism to the same extent as 19th century empires; it tends to prefers tributaries.<br /> <br /> [2] Specifically the Church of England and the Church of Scotland (the latter is not Anglican, btw). Not the Church in Wales, the Church of Ireland, the Scottish Episcopalians or any of the other provinces.<br /> <br /> [3] Even if it were, it would be hard to argue that that was the specific influence and not -- given Grabowski's statements -- the relationship between Qing Kangxi and Tibetan Buddhism.<br /> <br /> [4] All of these pale in comparison to Imperial Russia post-Peter the Great, where the Orthodox church wound up a government department in an absolutist state par excellance and contributed in the settler colonialist rampages around Siberia and the Cacausus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":978,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","user":"Iozz-Sothoth","date":". 05-09-2020, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T11:26:04-07:00","id":1387020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iozz-Sothoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1387017#post1387017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some observations: <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I miss when you posted more often.<br /> <br /> I find your disputes of my perspective and the manner in which I expressed it to be compelling, and shall consider those elements in the future. I can definitely see my comparison between the Immaculate Order and the Church of England to be one of those pithy one-liners I come to while reading some things and become too heavily attached to until effectively challenged on how much nuance they're leaving out.<br /> <br /> Cheers for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T11:55:05-07:00","id":1387030,"title":"","content":"Incredible. <br /> <br /> This was an informative, courteous, and polite debate on the internet which led to everyone involved more knowledgeable and better for it. <br /> <br /> Well done, sirs (without a hint of sarcasm)<br /> <br /> *claps*<br /> <br /> *claps*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:04:20-07:00","id":1387033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I miss when you posted more often. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you always have stuff to add in this kind of conversation Iozz.<br /> <br /> And this is the sort of conversation I enjoy with you, but some in our group get bored when we do in-game or in email, so we could do it here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, I could bring up some points or add some things or whatever, but as an Englishman who, despite being baptised in the kind of Church that the 19th century English government would legally bar me from public service for, does currently attend an Anglican Church (even if it's the barely Anglican kind), I maybe have some biases or whatever.<br /> <br /> So anyway, Isator seems happy with that, but if you want to continue do so, but otherwise I'm going to get back to the main thread topic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So yes, in my Creation the only kinds of Exalts who exist are Infernals, Lunars and Dragonblood. The Sidereals existed once, but were wiped from history by the Solars in the Usurpation. The Solars' spirits were trapped in Hell for 1500 years, and now they're all Infernals. Hearteaters, Umbrals, etc, were destroyed in the Titanomacy. Getimians and Liminals have just never existed. Alchemicals may exist, but Autocthon is sealed behind the Seal of Eight Divinities and they're with him.<br /> <br /> If Essence comes out and we switch to it, and someone wants to make a new character of one of these types, I might do a soft retcon and have them have existed, just that the PCs didn't know about them. Like a few Sidereals survived in secret, or whatever.<br /> Not Solars though.<br /> <br /> <br /> What have others done with types of Exalt? Especially the new ones for 3rd ed, ones we don't have rules for, etc, etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-09-2020, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:22:17-07:00","id":1387039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1387020#post1387020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I miss when you posted more often.<br /> <br /> I find your disputes of my perspective and the manner in which I expressed it to be compelling, and shall consider those elements in the future. I can definitely see my comparison between the Immaculate Order and the Church of England to be one of those pithy one-liners I come to while reading some things and become too heavily attached to until effectively challenged on how much nuance they're leaving out.<br /> <br /> Cheers for that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No worries! (I should probably post here more often tbh, but I have so little time these days.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T11:27:32-07:00","id":1387549,"title":"","content":"one of the things I use is that the cycle of death and rebirth are only broken because the neverborn are literally refusing to be reborn, if they let go of their fetters they would cycle through the well of souls and one of a few examples may happen. A generation in a region is born with horrific nightmares of battles long since fought and lost/won, dreams of glory and eons of shaping the cosmos come to them, then at the age they would be able to exalt at they instead start to feel a pull to a region that either already has a high level demesne or they start building one in a remote area. once the demesne is built or acquired the entire region starts to go through a metamorphosis and tons of essence coalescing the new primordial comes together with the &quot;mortals&quot; being it's new start of a pantheon<br /> <br /> the sids have seen this happen only once since the Usurpation and they stopped it before it was able to complete, they mistook it for a massive summoning and killed everyone/thing present along with dispersing the gathered essence. this process has not made it to completion since the gods were created","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T11:52:46-07:00","id":1387559,"title":"","content":"Huh, I can see some interesting stuff to do with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T13:01:33-07:00","id":1387576,"title":"","content":"In my Creation, the Twilight Caste aren't the bigtime sorcerers. That role belongs to the Eclipse Caste, to whom the role of Sorcerers fits much more naturally. Twilight Castes are sages, academics, architects, artificers, doctors, savants, detectives, and the like. They are the overwhelmingly intellectual Caste of the Solar Exalted. Sorcery is not an intellectual affair in Exalted, the way that magic is in many other games. Tying magic to study feels like a sacred cow of other rpgs brought over when Exalted was first written.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers in Exalted are mysterious and enigmatic figures who gain their powers through the trauma of the Wyld, or through pacts with Demons or Elementals, through bonds with powerful and strange items or places. The Eclipse Caste literally has an Anima Power that lets them seal bargains and make pacts with strange forces. It seems so obvious that Sorcery should be a thing that they're known for, rather than Twilights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T14:54:42-07:00","id":1387596,"title":"","content":"Tbh, in the game I used to run we've had 4 Eclipses... 1 spymaster, 1 author and 2 sorcerers. And no serious Twilight sorcerers (the Twilight had 1 terrestrial spell, but at Essence 5 that's barely a drop in the ocean). So in my experience, Eclipses are more commonly sorcerers than Twilights!<br /> And certainly the Pact with Mara, Pact with an Ifrit Lord, and many other initiations feel more Eclipsey than Twilighty. The only one that feels really Twilighty is the Heptagram one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T14:55:48-07:00","id":1387597,"title":"","content":"(Cackles softly, &quot;The invocation of dread Iozz-Sothoth, by exactly such topic shift as would summon that Outer God itself, was successful!&quot; ...<br /> <br /> I mean I totally expected that... Ahem, well anyway, definitely a better outcome of that conversation than whatever I would've blundered in with, half or more ignorant of my subject, in response.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T01:27:39-07:00","id":1389222,"title":"","content":"- The ruins of Rathess are within the borders of Ixcoatli, and it is a holy site to them. They (erroneously in the biological sense, but accurately in a cultural sense) claim the Dragon Kings they know relatively little of as their forbearers. They don\u2019t realize who the beastial claw striders in the jungle really are.<br /> <br /> - Coral is a matrilineal patriarchy with little sense of marriage. Men have little responsibility for their own kids, but rather for their sisters\u2019 kids. The patriarch of most children\u2019s homes are their maternal uncle, or maternal-maternal grand uncle.<br /> <br /> - Wavecrest has chain marriages with every individual allowed to take two spouses. There is cultural rhetoric about a single great chain, but this is not literally the case.<br /> <br /> - the river Elidad starts in the Fire Peaks near Gem and flows north to break into a fertile river delta at the sea that includes Lap. Kingdoms like Zephyr are spread up and down its annually flooding banks. Besides being Gem\u2019s main traderoute, it also is the course by which the Realm reinforces its legions through the Satrapies.<br /> <br /> - If the above evokes the Nile, than the river that flows from the Summer Mountains to the Dreaming Sea that Kamathahar sits upon should evoke the Niger, in how it forms the spine of the Prasadi Empire the way the Niger did the Mali, and allows for a capital so far inland while the bulk of its empire follows the river\u2019s course to the sea.<br /> <br /> - Creation has a slight curve, as all of it is built on the slopes of the Pole of Earth continuing outward and downward to form the fundament. Dawn in Wavecrest is roughly five hours after dawn in Ixcoatli.<br /> <br /> (this is necessary as the alternative is that on the flat plane, dawn is simultaneous everywhere, but morning is short and bright in the East followed by a loooong slow dimming evening, while the reverse would be the case in the West, with the brief evening as the brightest time of day. A curve allows everywhere to have the same length mornings and afternoons, but requires that they aren\u2019t simultaneous)<br /> <br /> - Creation\u2019s stable Pole Star always points centerward, not North. The dome of heaven turns on its yearly axis around the Imperial Mountain, as a literal axis mundi. This means all the known constellations are always in the sky together rather than rising and falling over the horizon. Relevant signs are thus highly influenced by where you are in Creation - as two children born the same night are born under different signs in different corners of Creation. Of course where the five planets (literally wandering stars) are among the constellations at any given time are of extreme importance to any given reading.<br /> <br /> Rename Shepherd of the Northstar as Shepherd of the Polestar","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-18-2020, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:18:52-07:00","id":1389657,"title":"","content":"I'm just running the Third Age. There was an ice age, a great flood, and now the Lunar PCs are in the Caucuses mountains, trading with the Amazons who live at the bottom of the River Don, and after they've found/fought a Clan Tepet Dragonblood next session, I think they'll be going to either the <i>urheimat</i> Iscomay, or Greece.<br /> <br /> Skytongue is Proto-Indo-European, Riverspeak is Proto-Semitic, Sumerian and ancient Kvart are Forestongue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-18-2020, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T18:25:42-07:00","id":1389807,"title":"","content":"Well, my Creation doesn't vary much, but can I talk about Autochthonia here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T19:32:28-07:00","id":1389826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1389807#post1389807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, my Creation doesn't vary much, but can I talk about Autochthonia here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is well within the purpose of this thread, but if not, no one's going to stop you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T19:44:23-07:00","id":1389828,"title":"","content":"To that effect *points at signature*. It\u2019s still 2e, but I\u2019ll update to 3e when the time comes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T00:07:47-07:00","id":1389884,"title":"","content":"Not much change here, but...<br /> First, my Creation is slightly curved. Solves a few interrogations about the horizon and daylight. Was Creation ever spherical in its existence? That's another question that I'm leaving open.<br /> Secondly, some mortal martial artists can use MA charms. It requires intense breathing exercise and whatever else the philosophy of the style may require, and help channel peripheral Essence since your chakras are otherwise closed, so to speak. It's not reliable, and only masters of a given style manage to pull this off on occasion, increasing their prestige. Only a true master can manage to briefly interact with the essence of the world and let out a true Terrifying Battle Shriek or pierce armor with their bare hands without breaking them. That being said? An Exalt beats them all the time. (This in small part helps justify the continued teaching of styles in mortal populations, and most importantly, helps give mortal masters some teeth beyond just having more dots to whack your face with a form weapon a little better, without negating the usefulness of being Exalted as a dedicated martial artist.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T00:59:28-07:00","id":1389891,"title":"","content":"In my creation, the Incarnae are the 7 souls of Gaia, and Creation is literally the grandest primordial, who was taken over by her children, the Primordials, and made into a slave. The Divine Rebellion was literally Creation revolting against its monstrous Primordial enslavers. When the Celestial Revolution ended, the Yozis broke their words and treaties in one very important way - they forced the Games of Divinity into Yu Shan, knowning the gods could not resist its addictive poison. Enraged, the 5 Incarnae left 5 proxies, and swore that Gaia the mother of Creation and true empress of all reality would never set foot in Creation again unless the Games were destroyed. Being that the treasonous, feckless gods of Yu Shan desired the games above all, and believed the lie that the winner of the games would be transformed into a Primordial if they won, the game was avidly played and all sorts of rationales were delivered. As a last insult, when the Solar purge was conducted, the Bronze faction cripped the Mask because Chepok Kejak dreamed of transcending to become a Primordial and ruling Yu Shan under his will, with only the Solar Exalted standing in the way. The Great Curse emanates from the games.<br /> <br /> The 7 Incarnae (Sol, Luna, Jupiter, Mars, Venus, Mercury and Saturn), who are the soul of Gaia, have resided outside of Creation in the deep Wyld, until now. Luna has always created Exalts at his whim, and now Sol calls to herself her old champions. These Exalts who are given the 2nd Breath directly by the true incarnae instead of their proxies are coordinated by Sol, who whispers to them in dreams and insulates them from the Great Curse, of which they are informed of. Needless to say, the Yozis and Malfeans regard the Proxied Solars (who can have their limit reduced by the intercession of a noble, courageous human adviser, who is immune to all of their charms) regard Gaia taking direct action as a dire threat. The Proxied Solars, Lunars and Sidereals are hunted even more than the usual escaped Celestial. Those who oppose Gaia fear her not just for selfish reasons - Sol, her shining heart, has warned that if Creation is not saved, she will need to take drastic action, recreate the world as a globe, and end the Age of Sorrows.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T02:04:16-07:00","id":1389897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1389891#post1389891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my creation, the Incarnae are the 7 souls of Gaia, and Creation is literally the grandest primordial, who was taken over by her children, the Primordials, and made into a slave. The Divine Rebellion was literally Creation revolting against its monstrous Primordial enslavers. When the Celestial Revolution ended, the Yozis broke their words and treaties in one very important way - they forced the Games of Divinity into Yu Shan, knowning the gods could not resist its addictive poison. Enraged, the 5 Incarnae left 5 proxies, and swore that Gaia the mother of Creation and true empress of all reality would never set foot in Creation again unless the Games were destroyed. Being that the treasonous, feckless gods of Yu Shan desired the games above all, and believed the lie that the winner of the games would be transformed into a Primordial if they won, the game was avidly played and all sorts of rationales were delivered. As a last insult, when the Solar purge was conducted, the Bronze faction cripped the Mask because Chepok Kejak dreamed of transcending to become a Primordial and ruling Yu Shan under his will, with only the Solar Exalted standing in the way. The Great Curse emanates from the games.<br /> <br /> The 7 Incarnae (Sol, Luna, Jupiter, Mars, Venus, Mercury and Saturn), who are the soul of Gaia, have resided outside of Creation in the deep Wyld, until now. Luna has always created Exalts at his whim, and now Sol calls to herself her old champions. These Exalts who are given the 2nd Breath directly by the true incarnae instead of their proxies are coordinated by Sol, who whispers to them in dreams and insulates them from the Great Curse, of which they are informed of. Needless to say, the Yozis and Malfeans regard the Proxied Solars (who can have their limit reduced by the intercession of a noble, courageous human adviser, who is immune to all of their charms) regard Gaia taking direct action as a dire threat. The Proxied Solars, Lunars and Sidereals are hunted even more than the usual escaped Celestial. Those who oppose Gaia fear her not just for selfish reasons - Sol, her shining heart, has warned that if Creation is not saved, she will need to take drastic action, recreate the world as a globe, and end the Age of Sorrows.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting and inspired take on Creation being a Primordial.<br /> <br /> I had an idea back in 2nd ed that I am on the fence over whether I will use it in 3rd ed that the Games of Divinity is such a sublime set up that the Primordials played it by using all their souls to kind of man their own stations. Primordials could use it to grow and develop, and Incarnae being usually singular beings play the games on a simpler level, but by the times of the World of Darkness the Unconquered Sun and Luna through the games transformed into Primordial like beings known as Celestines, and learned to develop their own sub souls which are Incarnae which can also create their own Avatars of high Jaggling level.<br /> <br /> But I always loved contemplating that Creation was a Sphere before the Divine Revolution, or like in Shards it was a Universal Spiral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T02:38:04-07:00","id":1389900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1389897#post1389897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting and inspired take on Creation being a Primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just realized that it makes me think of the latest developments of WoW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T10:22:28-07:00","id":1390001,"title":"","content":"The Immaculate religions do take the Immaculate Dragons literally. They arose allegorically in the Shogunate (the deeds of any Air DB seen as achieving unity with Mela were described in text as actions of Mela), but by the time the Order was founded after the Shogunate they were taken literally.<br /> <br /> A major religious difference between the Philosophy and the Faith, is the Immaculate Philosophy reaches the Elemental Dragons incarnated themselves as the Immaculate Dragons., while the Immaculate Faith teaches that they were \u201cnormal\u201d (though exceptional) Dragon-Blooded who achieved unity with the Elemental Dragons through their virtue and enlightened deeds showing the way for others.<br /> <br /> The ancestor worshipping heresy in the Riverlands that Charlie\u2019s follows plays off the Faith\u2019s take on the Deagons to pray to and honor ancestors believed to have achieved unity with the Dragons as retroactive incarnations of them. The door to ancestor worship opened they also honor the dead in the underworld as still pursuing their enlightenment, or as having achieved unity with the dragons but choosing to stay around as protective bodhisattva for their families.<br /> <br /> The Pure Way believes that Terrestrial Exaltation is literally the divine presence of the Elemental Dragons, thus making all DBs the literal presence of the divine, and that the Immaculate Dragons were the children of the Elemental Deagons conceived by the Elemental Essence itself in their Exalted mothers. This helps them branch the state of Terrestrial Exaltation with the honoring of God-Blood in the older Pure Way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T19:21:12-07:00","id":1390891,"title":"","content":"the whole cycle of creation is just how primordials reproduce. they've all done this so many times, with different ones providing different roles. One time it will be Malfeas himself that champions the Exalted alongside Gaia and the various realms will form until the infernals are produced and are able to unfurl brand new Primordials into the cosmos","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T01:41:09-07:00","id":1391147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1390891#post1390891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the whole cycle of creation is just how primordials reproduce. they've all done this so many times, with different ones providing different roles. One time it will be Malfeas himself that champions the Exalted alongside Gaia and the various realms will form until the infernals are produced and are able to unfurl brand new Primordials into the cosmos</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting but it seems very cynic as well, I think ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T01:45:21-07:00","id"