ser":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T03:25:59-07:00","id":1391658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1391575#post1391575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exaltations are a natural phenomenon and no one knows exactly how many of each exalt are active at any one time. The gods still take credit for them sure, but they are no more tied to a god than a wave is tied to a breeze over the ocean. they are just a consequence of the other. Solar exalted exist because the Sol exists, same for all exalts</div> </div> </div> </div>Do the gods sill choose who gets Exalted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T03:37:26-07:00","id":1391660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1391575#post1391575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exaltations are a natural phenomenon and no one knows exactly how many of each exalt are active at any one time. The gods still take credit for them sure, but they are no more tied to a god than a wave is tied to a breeze over the ocean. they are just a consequence of the other. Solar exalted exist because the Sol exists, same for all exalts</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me a little bit about my campaign introduction for the message to the Zenith which was bit &quot;off&quot; because he had still not reconcile with Creation, so the messsage was not actually a personnal one but a &quot;recorded one&quot; that dated back The First Age","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T15:36:40-07:00","id":1392067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1391658#post1391658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the gods sill choose who gets Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>they say they do to save face but no, the exaltation is completely free of the gods, the only thing that might erase an exaltation is if some how their corresponding deity were erased from existence, both past and present","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T00:45:29-07:00","id":1392142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1392067#post1392067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> they say they do to save face but no, the exaltation is completely free of the gods, the only thing that might erase an exaltation is if some how their corresponding deity were erased from existence, both past and present</div> </div> </div> </div>Do the gods of a specific exigent still die when he is Exalted ? Or does he die and someone &quot;random&quot; (maybe the sister or rival of the one he wanted to uplift) can get Exalted instead ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T08:28:30-07:00","id":1392197,"title":"","content":"Okay so my Creation is more a presentational quirk than anything I'm doing drastically different in terms of world building.<br /> <br /> While I didn't like last edition's industrialisation of magic, science is nevertheless pretty important to how I present my game world. When I say \u201cscience\u201d I mean there's a lot of observation and experimentation with natural (and supernatural) phenomena, rather than modern amenities that the players take for granted being supplied by magic that's wearing the trappings of science.<br /> <br /> I could go into detail but other people have given their preferences and I don't want to shit on them. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T08:39:36-07:00","id":1392208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1392197#post1392197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so my Creation is more a presentational quirk than anything I'm doing drastically different in terms of world building.<br /> <br /> While I didn't like last edition's industrialisation of magic, science is nevertheless pretty important to how I present my game world. When I say \u201cscience\u201d I mean there's a lot of observation and experimentation with natural (and supernatural) phenomena, rather than modern amenities that the players take for granted being supplied by magic that's wearing the trappings of science.<br /> <br /> I could go into detail but other people have given their preferences and I don't want to shit on them. <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>So, obviously I can't speak for everyone, but as someone whose preferences are different, I'd still love to hear more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T19:35:50-07:00","id":1392393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1392142#post1392142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do the gods of a specific exigent still die when he is Exalted ? Or does he die and someone &quot;random&quot; (maybe the sister or rival of the one he wanted to uplift) can get Exalted instead ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question, hadn't thought about it. I'd say it doesn't permanently kill them, they expend their essence into the natural tapestry of creation, energetically screaming their story, their legend into the fabric of creation to form an exigent exaltation, this is extraordinary taxing on the god and can result in weaker gods dissolving into their legends for centuries until they have enough strength to separate themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T19:37:51-07:00","id":1392395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1392197#post1392197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so my Creation is more a presentational quirk than anything I'm doing drastically different in terms of world building.<br /> <br /> While I didn't like last edition's industrialisation of magic, science is nevertheless pretty important to how I present my game world. When I say \u201cscience\u201d I mean there's a lot of observation and experimentation with natural (and supernatural) phenomena, rather than modern amenities that the players take for granted being supplied by magic that's wearing the trappings of science.<br /> <br /> I could go into detail but other people have given their preferences and I don't want to shit on them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I second JohnDoe244, please share, I never know what new inspiration I will in someone else's ideas and thoughts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T00:00:19-07:00","id":1392427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1392197#post1392197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so my Creation is more a presentational quirk than anything I'm doing drastically different in terms of world building.<br /> <br /> While I didn't like last edition's industrialisation of magic, science is nevertheless pretty important to how I present my game world. When I say \u201cscience\u201d I mean there's a lot of observation and experimentation with natural (and supernatural) phenomena, rather than modern amenities that the players take for granted being supplied by magic that's wearing the trappings of science.<br /> <br /> I could go into detail but other people have given their preferences and I don't want to shit on them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Supporting others here for more details ! I live for the destruction of magitech ! (Joking of course)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T08:15:37-07:00","id":1392541,"title":"","content":"Mortal sorcerers, while not exactly common, are extremely widespread. Most major townships have one lurking at the boundaries, and cities can and do have small cabals.<br /> <br /> This is thematically because I like to use sorcery as a metaphor for the equalizing and alienating power of knowledge and education, partly because that means Exalted always have at least one rival who might be on their level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T11:27:18-07:00","id":1392607,"title":"","content":"I go with rarer myself, since I tend to run with some of the game biggest fictional insprations to infomr things. So the for sorcery I have been using myself has been what is hinted at in <b>The Black Comapny</b>. There are minor sorcerers about, and a kingdom might actually have a court sourcerer. Sometimes that sorcerer might not even be one officially on paper (like Smoke in the later books). And concentrations of more than two ro three is notable in how much well, power, that is in one spot. Or if htey're dedicated, do weird shit that builds up like Bomanz in the releasing of the Lady or the necromancer in the recent <b>Port of Shadows</b> intersequel.<br /> <br /> Another is to me Tales to the Flat Earth, where there are scholars and sorcerers, but are a notable amount of folks who think they're magic (and not) and folks who have potential fo rmagic (but don't relaize it). Sorcerers there are not common enough to be ordinary, but not rare enough to be unheard of basically. Enough there are the myriad sorcerous initaitons, but that having more than one or two in a polity means a lot.<br /> <br /> Or they could be Lisa Tepes from the <b>Castlevania </b> animated series, where she's not relaly a mage at all (she's Medicine and Lore in Exalted contexts) but the uninformed/uneducated won't know the difference if you do enough things that work. And the local medicine woman's soultions aren't shit but are probably running on some half-known occult principles.<br /> <br /> I guess for me it is a genre thing. It's also admit it is a bit of a philosophical thing. I think meritocracy i n general is a lie that the powerful create to make themselves feel justified in keeping others down. So I'm not oen to go and put actulal in-setting &quot;rewards&quot; to folks who work really hard, when I think a lot of power and success is down to luck and circumstance as much if not more than inherent ability. There's a lot of folks who could have been good sorcerers who never got a chance, adn a lot of folks who had all the chance who are good at being a quack basically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T16:51:52-07:00","id":1392698,"title":"","content":"In my creation Eye and Seven Despairs is almost a completely different character, tossing out anything 2e edition said to use the 1e incarnation as a baseline.<br /> <br /> I know he's going full-on gothic mad scientist this edition, and while I found the idea of him playing his deathknights against each other and 'himself' as he did neat, I found the 'posing as his own concubine' stuff a little too squicky for me (and likely my group), and had the thought that perhaps Star of Dirt and Doubt was always the real Eye and Seven Despairs, and used the mummy as a puppet she could possess so that she could do her experiments without being interrupted, and used the deathknights as a way to retire the puppet so she could focus on her work without needing to run the kingdom herself. Now she's basically Liv Octavius from Into the Spiderverse as a gothic mad scientist with a trio of lovers running her kingdom for her while she &quot;recreates their former master's studies&quot;.<br /> <br /> I also ditched the 'Games of Divinity are addictive' plot, only the Unconquered Sun is addicted to them, and only because he's using them as a crutch for his depression after the 1st age went so wrong, basically the Thor plot from Endgame. Luna is splitting their attention between disguising themself as various minor spirits both in creation and heaven to aid the lunars without openly contradicting the mandate of heaven, oppose the bureaucracy of heaven without openly condemning it (at the urging of the maidens), while also trying to support the US and keeping the lighthouse lit for Gaia's return. The Maidens are doing exactly as they say they should be, not even the sidereals know why that has led to inaction in heaven for so long, some think it's to place the sidereals in charge of heaven, now with the return of the solars exalted new theories have emerged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T04:39:29-07:00","id":1394755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1392208#post1392208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, obviously I can't speak for everyone, but as someone whose preferences are different, I'd still love to hear more.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1392395#post1392395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> I second JohnDoe244, please share, I never know what new inspiration I will in someone else's ideas and thoughts</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1392427#post1392427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Supporting others here for more details ! I live for the destruction of magitech ! (Joking of course)</div> </div> </div> </div> I try to maintain a good general knowledge of how people did things before the post-industrial era (and what they were shockingly close to doing if they'd known where to look) because that's more likely to impress the players than an artefact that's a modern convenience with the serial numbers filed off.<br /> For example, I've found that players are by and large more impressed by the use of yakhch\u0101ls and ice houses, a pretty low-tech solutions for storing ice that's out of season than Winterbreath Jars. Even if these Winterbreath Jars are being produced by mortal artificers there's still potentially this sense that they're not innovating and simply copying a more advanced design that they're incapable of improving upon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T11:44:55-07:00","id":1395118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1394755#post1394755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I try to maintain a good general knowledge of how people did things before the post-industrial era (and what they were shockingly close to doing if they'd known where to look) because that's more likely to impress the players than an artefact that's a modern convenience with the serial numbers filed off.<br /> For example, I've found that players are by and large more impressed by the use of yakhch\u0101ls and ice houses, a pretty low-tech solutions for storing ice that's out of season than Winterbreath Jars. Even if these Winterbreath Jars are being produced by mortal artificers there's still potentially this sense that they're not innovating and simply copying a more advanced design that they're incapable of improving upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>thats awesome, I've just started learning about earth bag homes and a few other things, you would be surprised how complex someone could make a home out of basically clay and soil","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T08:55:12-07:00","id":1398606,"title":"","content":"In my Creation, Solars get to hear... sort of a *Mantra* of exaltation, the *idea* of their Caste, imbued by the Unconquered Sun upon creation. And the Lunar Bond was a mostly informal thing already, before they *-ified* it into something more distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","name":"Aquatica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T18:34:38-07:00","id":1399713,"title":"","content":"can't remember if I posted this or not before<br /> <br /> Exaltations don't have a fixed number in my creation, the numbers given are rough estimates based on how many people in creation have the ability and the opportunity to exalt at any given time, any hard numbers are just popaganda","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T05:19:31-07:00","id":1399793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1399713#post1399713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can't remember if I posted this or not before<br /> <br /> Exaltations don't have a fixed number in my creation, the numbers given are rough estimates based on how many people in creation have the ability and the opportunity to exalt at any given time, any hard numbers are just popaganda</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it that's a good idea","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T17:38:32-07:00","id":1405701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1377439#post1377439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We already have this in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/65219-your-headcanon\">Your Headcanon Thread.</a><br /> <br /> But my changes, I'm a bit more free form with how I display Godblooded, if I want I may have the Children of mighty beings sometimes display Exalted like strength.<br /> <br /> And My Creation may actually be more like a coin then a plane, and the otherside is more a wild Pangea without humans or Gods but with lots of dinosaurs, and maybe elementals. Humans and spirits would have to be stranded here to start up a population. Though sometimes I think I may change it so its more the bottom layer of the deep below Creation, as I have it the Primordials would just plop new layers on Creation in the past anytime they wanted a tableau rasa.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now i'm thinking of &quot;Flipside&quot; as a place the disappeared Primordials exiled themselves upon with some key loyalists and creations to start anew, so to speak. The Ebon Dragon and Szoreny might know and have some contact, have to take some time with the kinks of the concept, but who knows, maybe worth a try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-31-2020, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T19:09:28-07:00","id":1405723,"title":"","content":"Hmm, human loyalists (like Autochthon took with him)? or Inhuman races?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T20:15:42-07:00","id":1405727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1405723#post1405723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, human loyalists (like Autochthon took with him)? or Inhuman races?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty good question, maybe a bit of both even, on a riff of the Human-Dragon King dynamic from before the Exalted.<br /> <br /> Main hurdle in my head is thinking of a reason for the Incarnae or Exalted not finding out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-31-2020, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T02:36:02-07:00","id":1405767,"title":"","content":"nevermind, misunderstood the question<br /> <br /> why can't we delete posts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T10:49:32-07:00","id":1405811,"title":"","content":"Firearms exist in very limited quantities.<br /> <br /> The shards of Shards of the Exalted Dream exist <i>alongside</i> &quot;regular&quot; Creation, and those who wander too far into the wyld can accidentally have an out-of-body experience inside one of them. A Chosen of Endings of mine came across Modern Exalted this way and fell in love with rock music. Later, a Solar ended up accidentally appearing in Gunstar and got the idea to try to contact Autochthonia from it. (His Twilight circlemate learning that she was like an uneducated grade schooler in comparison to Gunstar's Twilights and getting miles of literal homework from them had mixed feelings on the matter)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 08-01-2020, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T12:24:05-07:00","id":1405823,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of giving something like guns to Autochthonians. Back when we first saw then in 1E the devs gave them crossbows, which were stated to not exist in Creation, to give them an exclusive type of weapon. However, since later 1E they've basically been made a common part of the setting making Autochthonian use of them no longer distinguishing. SO I think some sort of firearm, like a pneumatic rifle pr something, would be great to give them a unique feel again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T13:32:53-07:00","id":1405828,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Firedust and Flamepieces/Firewands are &quot;just&quot; regular early firearms, mainly because I like the association of Lead with Saturn as &quot;the metal of Endings&quot; too much to ignore it, and feel the revelation of actual realistic cannons existing in Creation as per Arms of the Chosen to be vindication enough. As for why they dont dominate warfare across Creation..... too expensive to make, since the springs and stuff in locks require high levels of technical skill and valuable materials (Spring-steel isn't cheap or easy to work with in a pre-industrial setting, much less gunbarrels that won't explode like pipe-bombs when exposed to drastic increases in pressure).</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T16:30:24-07:00","id":1405852,"title":"","content":"locks like that are only necessary for advanced firearms like wheel-locks and flint-locks. simple matchlocks can be made with simpler mechanisms that don't use springs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T17:29:48-07:00","id":1405856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1405852#post1405852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">locks like that are only necessary for advanced firearms like wheel-locks and flint-locks. simple matchlocks can be made with simpler mechanisms that don't use springs</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone remember princess mononoke. Modern firearms are hard to make. But that doesn't mean guns weren't around for quite some time. <br /> <br /> It just means that if you wanna go rambo, you gotta be an exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T18:26:53-07:00","id":1405862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1405852#post1405852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">locks like that are only necessary for advanced firearms like wheel-locks and flint-locks. simple matchlocks can be made with simpler mechanisms that don't use springs</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but then I have to come up with a rationale for why the Realm and Lookshy aren't rompin-stompin Pike-and-Shot militaries, as opposed to the quasi-Roman/Chinese spear-and-arrow things they are in-lore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T19:23:09-07:00","id":1405864,"title":"","content":"Why spend the money equiping mere mortals so well when the real strength comes from the Exalted officer corp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T19:33:17-07:00","id":1405865,"title":"","content":"Why spend the money equiping mere mortals so well when the real strength comes from the Exalted officer corp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T20:18:58-07:00","id":1405872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1405865#post1405865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why spend the money equiping mere mortals so well when the real strength comes from the Exalted officer corp?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think muskets are often cheaper than bows. Or possibly they require less training, which makes fielding a force of musket-wielders cheaper than fielding a force of bow-wielders.<br /> My impression is that early muskets were in fact a less effective weapon than bows - the ability to be fielded cheaply was often the main advantage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T21:06:28-07:00","id":1405877,"title":"","content":"it was more the training factor. a gun is more expensive as it requires smithing and woodworking, whereas a longbow only need certain woodworking. Bows were more effective at longer ranges until the 1800s, but no army wanted to field both so they went with more power at closer ranges and ease of training.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T05:28:05-07:00","id":1405920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1405864#post1405864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why spend the money equiping mere mortals so well when the real strength comes from the Exalted officer corp?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Exalts are rare, and every single change that lets mortals hold their own instead of depending on their Dragonblooded Officers lets the Dragonblooded do something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T08:42:23-07:00","id":1405950,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah. And another thing. <br /> <br /> The Realm would *love* Gunpowder. And Cannons. <br /> <br /> Gunpowder cannons shifted the balance of power to centralized rule for many reasons. For starters, only those who already have immense amounts of wealth and resources can mass produce gunpowder and the metal required for making those city-busting cannons. And only those with dedicated education systems are able to produce the mathematicians required for an artillery corps. And the few places that can *defend* against artillery? Expensive starforts that require tons of earth. <br /> <br /> Guess which place in Creation has the best education system, enough technological know-how to produce cannons and gunpowder en masse, and has mass literacy to calculate vectors? <br /> <br /> The realm. <br /> <br /> The introduction of Gunpowder would mean that the Realm would make like European powers smashing their way against the unlucky natives of the world (at least, more than usual). Gatling Guns aimed at hordes of barbarians clad only in animal skins and leathers. And of course, Dragonblooded Officers leading and firing out entire hordes of cannons and artillery at unlucky souls (Dragonblooded can boost the competence of the people around them as their excellency alone), turning entire battalions into mincemeat and tearing apart entire fortresses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T17:36:49-07:00","id":1406022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1405872#post1405872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think muskets are often cheaper than bows. Or possibly they require less training, which makes fielding a force of musket-wielders cheaper than fielding a force of bow-wielders.<br /> My impression is that early muskets were in fact a less effective weapon than bows - the ability to be fielded cheaply was often the main advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, the exact opposite. Even a smoothbore matchlock musket is going to be more accurate, at longer ranges, with greater killing power, than a bow. You can read quotes straight from military officers all across 1500s Europe stating as such.<br /> <br /> The Native Americans didn't drop bows liike last years New Years Resolution because guns were <i>&quot;worse&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1405877#post1405877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Bows were more effective at longer ranges until the 1800s, but no army wanted to field both so they went with more power at closer ranges and ease of training.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haaa.....<i>no, </i>not really. <br /> <br /> Contrary to what the history-memes say, a wooden bow (without modern sighting equipment, that is) isn't really usable for accurate fire past 50 or so feet. And past that, even smoothbore guns are more effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","user":"Boston123","date":". 08-02-2020, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T17:40:43-07:00","id":1406023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1405950#post1405950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah. And another thing.<br /> <br /> The Realm would *love* Gunpowder. And Cannons.<br /> <br /> Gunpowder cannons shifted the balance of power to centralized rule for many reasons. For starters, only those who already have immense amounts of wealth and resources can mass produce gunpowder and the metal required for making those city-busting cannons. And only those with dedicated education systems are able to produce the mathematicians required for an artillery corps. And the few places that can *defend* against artillery? Expensive starforts that require tons of earth.<br /> <br /> Guess which place in Creation has the best education system, enough technological know-how to produce cannons and gunpowder en masse, and has mass literacy to calculate vectors?<br /> <br /> The realm.<br /> <br /> The introduction of Gunpowder would mean that the Realm would make like European powers smashing their way against the unlucky natives of the world (at least, more than usual). Gatling Guns aimed at hordes of barbarians clad only in animal skins and leathers. And of course, Dragonblooded Officers leading and firing out entire hordes of cannons and artillery at unlucky souls (Dragonblooded can boost the competence of the people around them as their excellency alone), turning entire battalions into mincemeat and tearing apart entire fortresses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of me wonders how sweet an Exalted Shard set in the 1600-1800s would be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T18:13:39-07:00","id":1406026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1406023#post1406023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of me wonders how sweet an Exalted Shard set in the 1600-1800s would be</div> </div> </div> </div>Steampunk Dragonblooded is a go! <br /> <br /> You already have an entrenched artistocracy. Just have a few autocthonians mixup with them here and there. And you can have a free cold war thrown in!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T23:24:01-07:00","id":1406069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1405701#post1405701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And now i'm thinking of &quot;Flipside&quot; as a place the disappeared Primordials exiled themselves upon with some key loyalists and creations to start anew, so to speak. The Ebon Dragon and Szoreny might know and have some contact, have to take some time with the kinks of the concept, but who knows, maybe worth a try.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this because Infernals could end conversations with each other with &quot;Catch you on the Flipside&quot; in addition to &quot;See you in Hell.&quot; <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T00:19:46-07:00","id":1406073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1406069#post1406069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this because Infernals could end conversations with each other with &quot;Catch you on the Flipside&quot; in addition to &quot;See you in Hell.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's that for certain, I think my main mental hurdle overall is &quot;Do i need a whole other world, hidden but accesible? For what kind of stories that i wouldn't tell of Creation?&quot;<br /> At least for now. Who knows what weird ideas might come up into my mind later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-05-2025, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T01:45:31-07:00","id":1406080,"title":"","content":"The main use I see in an entirely new world is to have one or more factions that can't really co-exist with the Scarlet Empire, being in a blank spot on the map only goes so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T09:11:58-07:00","id":1406120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary?p=1406080#post1406080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main use I see in an entirely new world is to have one or more factions that can't really co-exist with the Scarlet Empire, being in a blank spot on the map only goes so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but couldn't an isle/sanctum/freehold or something of the sort work for that? Upside down world involves a certain degree of extra separation - and room to throw stuff, as it is sort of a whole new Creation. I guess wrapping up my head around the scale - or what would i use it for - is the part where i'm stumbling a bit for now.<br /> <br /> Maybe after i come up with some crazy homebrewed ur-empire that could not exist in Creation without being a major threat to the Scarlet Empire's existence.<br /> <br /> (Actually, i do have one of these, but it is <b><i>very intentionally</i></b> set in the Middlemarches to Deep Wyld, as it involves that one Solar with Wyld Shaping that manages to escape everybody and flourish for ages out there)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}